.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPYRUN
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPYRUN'.
Run Python Script via Qshell - Help
:p.The Run Python Script via Qshell (QSHPYRUN) command is used to run a Python script
via QSHEXEC and log the results appropriately.
:p.The following example calls a helloworld.py script that write to STDOUT.
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPYRUN SCRIPTDIR('/pythonapps')
   SCRIPTFILE('hello.py')
   ARGS(Parm1 Parm2)
   PYVERSION(3)
   DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
   LOGSTDOUT(*NO)
   PRTSTDOUT(*NO)
   DLTSTDOUT(*YES)
   IFSSTDOUT(*NO)
   IFSFILE('/tmp/log.txt')
   IFSOPT(*REPLACE)
   PRTSPLF(QSHPYRUN)
   PRTUSRDTA(*NONE)
   PRTTXT(*NONE)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHPYRUN/SCRIPTDIR'.
Python script directory (SCRIPTDIR) - Help
:xh3.Python script directory (SCRIPTDIR)
:p.The IFS directory location for the Python script. :hp2.Ex: /python:ehp2.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/SCRIPTFILE'.
Python script file name (SCRIPTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Python script file name (SCRIPTFILE)
:p.The script file name you want to call without the directory path.
The QSHPYRUN command puts it all together. :hp2.Ex: hello.py:ehp2.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/ARGS'.
Python command line arguments (ARGS) - Help
:xh3.Python command line arguments (ARGS)
:p.Command line parameter argument list.
:p.Up to 40 - 200 byte argument/parameter values can be passed to a Python script call.
:P.Each parm is automatically trimmed. Do NOT put double quotes around the parms or your program call
may get errors because your parameters get compromised with extra double quotes.
:P.The double quotes are already added automatically inside the CL command processing program.
Single quotes are allowed around your parmaeter data though if desired:
:hp2.Ex: 'My Parm Value 1' 'My Parm Value 2':ehp2.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/ARGDLM'.
Command line arg delimiter (ARGDLM) - Help
:xh3.Command line arg delimiter (ARGDLM)
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DBLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Double quotes are used to delimit the command line arguments.
:pt.:pk.*SGLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Single quotes are used to delimit the command line arguments.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No delimiter is used.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PYVERSION'.
Python version (PYVERSION) - Help
:xh3.Python version (PYVERSION)
:p.Specifies the Python version to use to run the script.
It should be set to either 2 or 2.7 for Python 2 or 3, 3.6 or 3.9 for Python 3.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PYPATH'.
Python bin path (PYPATH) - Help
:xh3.Python bin path (PYPATH)
:p.The this is the directory path to your Python binaries (python/python3).
:p.Hopefully you have already installed the Yum versions so the default path should be good.
Leave value set to *DEFAULT. Default= /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin.
The default path lives in the PYPATH data area in the PYONI library.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/USEVENV'.
Use virtual environment (USEVENV) - Help
:xh3.Use virtual environment (USEVENV)
:p.Use virtual environment.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Run your Python script using an existing Python virtual environment as
specified in the Python virtual environment path.
The IFS directory and virtual environment must exist.
:p.
:hp2.Note: When using virtual environment, you will need to make sure the PYPATH
data area value is set to ' ' or pass ' ' to the PYPATH parameter to make sure the system level
python binary does not picked up. Each venv has its own python executable:ehp2.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not use a virtual environment.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/OUTFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/OUTFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/MBROPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/MBROPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/PASEJOBNAM'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PASEJOBNAM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/DEBUGCMD'.
Debug QSHEXEC command (DEBUGCMD) - Help
:xh3.Debug QSHEXEC command (DEBUGCMD)
:parml.
:p.This parameter allows you to debug the command line that QSHPYRUN will run via QSHEXEC.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If set to *YES, your job must be running interactively and it will display the command line
that QSHPYRUN composed to execute via QSHEXEC before it runs.
:p.This is good for debugging or you are curious what the exec QSHEXEC command will look like.
Under the covers QSHPYRUN utilizes the QSHEXEC command to run the Python command line.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not debug the command line.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/CHGSCRDIR'.
Change to script directory (CHGSCRDIR) - Help
:xh3.Change to script directory (CHGSCRDIR)
:p.Specifies whether to change the current working directory to the script directory
before running the script.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not change the current working directory.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Change the current working directory to the script directory.
:eparml.
:ehelp.


.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHLOGSCAN
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHLOGSCAN'.
Scan the stdout outfile for the selected value - Help
:p.This CL command is a convenience command that can be used to scan a
STDOUT log for a specific value to indicate success or failure.
:p.The following example scans the outfile log in file QTEMP/STDOUTQSH for a
text value of :hp3.successfully:ehp3. somewhere in any line of the log file output:
:XMP.
:hp2.
MONMSG MSGID(CPF9898) EXEC(DO)
SNDPGMMSG MSG('Did not find string of success in program output.') TOUSR(RICHARD)
ENDDO
QSHLOGSCAN SCANFOR('successfully')
EXACTMATCH(*NO)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLOGSCAN/SCANFOR'.
Value to scan for (SCANFOR) - Help
:xh3.Value to scan for (SCANFOR)
:p.Text value to scan for on each line in the stdout outfile.
:p.The value passed IS case sensitive and must match the value in the log file.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLOGSCAN/EXACTMATCH'.
Exact match-*YES, Contains-*NO (EXACTMATCH) - Help
:xh3.Exact match-*YES, Contains-*NO (EXACTMATCH)
:p.Exact match-*YES, Contains-*NO
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.At least one line must contain the value somewhere in the line.
Good for generic matching.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Value must match exactly and be the only thing on the selected line.
:eparml.
:ehelp.


.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHQRYTMP
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHQRYTMP'.
SQL Query Data to Temp Table - Help
:p.This CL command is a convenience command that can be used to run an
SQL data selection query and create an outfile of resulting data.
:NT.
The command returns a CPF9898 escape message on error. Otherwise a CPF9898 completion message.
:ENT.
:p.The following example queries all the records from table QIWS/QCUSCTDT and
places the result in to an output table named: SQLTMP0001 in library QTEMP.
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHQRYTMP SQL('SELECT * FROM QIWS/QCUSTCDT')
    OUTFILE(SQLTMP0001)
    EMPTYERROR(*YES)
    PROMPT(*NO)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
The following data areas are auto-created in the current job library QTEMP to track resulting query info.
You can retreive a resulting record count or the name of the outfile to check for existence
in case it didn't get created for some reason such as query failure.
:XMP.
:hp2.
SQLQRYCNT - Query result record count.
SQLQRYFIL - Output file created by the query.
SQLQRYLIB - Output file library for the file created by the query.
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/SQL'.
SQL query (SQL) - Help
:xh3.SQL query (SQL)
:p.Enter an SQL SELECT statement to query some specific data.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/PARMS'.
SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS) - Help
:xh3.SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS)
:p.Enter up to 30 parameter placeholder values you want to replace dynamically
in your SQL statements at runtime. These are not required if you don't want to
dynamic parameter replacement.
:p.Ex: :hp2.@@LIB:ehp2. for library or :hp2.@@FILE:ehp2. for file.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/PARMVALS'.
SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS) - Help
:xh3.SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS)
:p.Enter up to 30 replacement values you want to replace dynamically in your SQL statements
at runtime. These values correspond with each placeholder value you set in the list of PARMS.
These are not required if you don't want to dynamic parameter replacement.
:p.Ex: :hp2.QIWS:ehp2. for library or :hp2.QCUSTCDT:ehp2. for file.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/OUTFILE'.
Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.This is the output file/table where data gets selected in to via an SQL query.
The table will get automatically created as a result of the query if it doesn't exist.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/OUTFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/EMPTYERROR'.
Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR) - Help
:xh3.Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR)
:p.This parameter determines whether a CPF9898 escape message is thrown if no records were selected by the q
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Throw escape message if no records were selected.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not throw escape message if no records were selected.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/NAMING'.
Naming (NAMING) - Help
:xh3.Naming (NAMING)
:p.This parameter determines what format your queries are using: *SYS or *SQL.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SYS:epk.
:pd.Use system naming convention for SQL queries.
:pt.:pk.*SQL:epk.
:pd.Use SQL naming convention for SQL queries.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/PROMPT'.
Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether to prompt the RUNSQL command before running.
Only use this parameter in an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not prompt the RUNSQL command.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Prompt the RUNSQL command.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/CRTIDCOL'.
Create row identity column (CRTIDCOL) - Help
:xh3.Create row identity column (CRTIDCOL)
:p.Specifies whether to allow adding of a unique identity column to your outfile table after it's created.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not add an identity column.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Add an identity column.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/IDCOLNAME'.
Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME) - Help
:xh3.Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME)
:p.Specifies the name of the identity column to add if CRTIDCOL is *YES.
RECID is the default name.
:ehelp.


.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHQRYSRC
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHQRYSRC'.
SQL Query Source to Temp Table - Help
:p.This CL command is a convenience command that can be used to run an SQL
data selection query and create an outfile of resulting data.
Instead of an SQL input statement parameter, the query pulls SQL source from a source member or IFS file mem
:NT.
The command returns a CPF9898 escape message on error. Otherwise a CPF9898 completion message.
:ENT.
:p.The following example queries all the records from table QIWS/QCUSCTDT and
places the result in to an output table named: SQLTMP0001 in library QTEMP.
It also replaces the selected placeholder parameters values in the SQL query that gets read from the source
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHQRYSRC SQLLOC(*SRCMBR)
    SRCFILE(QSHONI/SOURCE)
    SRCMBR(SQLTEST3)
    PARMS(@@LIB @@file)
    PARMVALS(qiws qcustcdt)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
The following data areas are auto-created in the current job library QTEMP to track resulting query info.
You can retreive a resulting record count or the name of the outfile to check for existence
in case it didn't get created for some reason such as query failure.
:XMP.
:hp2.
SQLQRYCNT - Query result record count.
SQLQRYFIL - Output file created by the query.
SQLQRYLIB - Output file library for the file created by the query.
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/SQLLOC'.
SQL source from location type (SQLLOC) - Help
:xh3.SQL source from location type (SQLLOC)
:p.This parameter determines if the SQL query is sourced from a source member or an IFS file. Default is *SR
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SRCMBR:epk.
:pd.The SQL query is sourced from a source physical file member.
:pt.:pk.*IFSFILE:epk.
:pd.The SQL query is sourced from an IFS file member.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/SRCFILE'.
SQL source file (SRCFILE) - Help
:xh3.SQL source file (SRCFILE)
:p.This is the source file that contains the SQL query source member if SQLLOC is *SRCMBR.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the SQL source file.
:PT.:PK.library-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the SQL source file is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/SRCMBR'.
Source member (SRCMBR) - Help
:xh3.Source member (SRCMBR)
:p.This is the source member that contains the SQL query if SQLLOC is *SRCMBR.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/IFSFILE'.
SQL IFS source file (IFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.SQL IFS source file (IFSFILE)
:p.This is the IFS file that contains the SQL query if SQLLOC is *IFSFILE.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/PARMS'.
SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS) - Help
:xh3.SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS)
:p.Enter up to 30 parameter placeholder values you want to replace dynamically
in your SQL statements at runtime. These are not required if you don't want to
dynamic parameter replacement.
:p.Ex: :hp2.@@LIB:ehp2. for library or :hp2.@@FILE:ehp2. for file.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/PARMVALS'.
SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS) - Help
:xh3.SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS)
:p.Enter up to 30 replacement values you want to replace dynamically in your SQL statements
at runtime. These values correspond with each placeholder value you set in the list of PARMS.
These are not required if you don't want to dynamic parameter replacement.
:p.Ex: :hp2.QIWS:ehp2. for library or :hp2.QCUSTCDT:ehp2. for file.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/OUTFILE'.
Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.This is the output file/table where data gets selected in to via an SQL query.
The table will get automatically created as a result of the query if it doesn't exist.
:P.
The possible values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.SQLTMP0001:EPK.
:PD.
The SQLTMP0001 table is created in the QTEMP library by default.
:P.
:PT.:PK.database-file-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name (library-name/database-file) of the temporary database file to create.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.QTEMP library is used for the temporary database file.
:PT.:PK.library-name:EPK.
:PD.Specify the name (library-name/database-file) of the temporary database file to create.
:EPARML.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/EMPTYERROR'.
Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR) - Help
:xh3.Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR)
:p.This parameter determines whether a CPF9898 escape message is thrown if no records were selected by the q
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Throw escape message if no records were selected.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not throw escape message if no records were selected.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/NAMING'.
Naming (NAMING) - Help
:xh3.Naming (NAMING)
:p.This parameter determines what format your queries are using: *SYS or *SQL.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SYS:epk.
:pd.Use system naming convention for SQL queries.
:pt.:pk.*SQL:epk.
:pd.Use SQL naming convention for SQL queries.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/PROMPT'.
Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether to prompt the RUNSQL command before running.
Only use this parameter in an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not prompt the RUNSQL command.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Prompt the RUNSQL command.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/CRTIDCOL'.
Create row identity column (CRTIDCOL) - Help
:xh3.Create row identity column (CRTIDCOL)
:p.Specifies whether to allow adding of a unique identity column to your outfile table after it's created.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not add an identity column.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Add an identity column.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/IDCOLNAME'.
Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME) - Help
:xh3.Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME)
:p.Specifies the name of the identity column to add if CRTIDCOL is *YES.
RECID is the default name.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/DLTTMPSRC'.
Delete temp source file after (DLTTMPSRC) - Help
:xh3.Delete temp source file after (DLTTMPSRC)
:p.Determines if the temporary source member TMPQRYSRC created in temporary source file 
QTEMP/TMPQRYSRC gets deleted after query processing.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Delete the temporary source member after query processing.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not delete the temporary source member after query processing.
:eparml.
:ehelp.


.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPATH
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPATH'.
Set Open Source Package Path (QSHPATH) - Help
:p.This CL command is a convenience command to add the IBM i Open Source packages directory name to the PATH
environment variable.
:P.The following example adds the default open source packages directory to the beginning of the PATH:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPATH PKGPATH(*DEFAULT)
        PATHLOC(*BEGIN)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPATH/PKGPATH'.
Open Source package path (PKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Open Source package path (PKGPATH)
:p.Specify IFS location to open source packages.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DEFAULT:epk.
:pd.The default value is /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin.
:pt.:pk.character-value:epk.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path to the open source packages directory.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPATH/PATHLOC'.
Open source path location (PATHLOC) - Help
:xh3.Open source path location (PATHLOC)
:p.Specify where the open source packages are placed in the PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DTAARA:epk.
:pd.The PATH location is retrieved from the data area in named QSHONI/QSHPATHLOC.
:pt.:pk.*BEGIN:epk.
:pd.Open source package path is prepended to the beginning of PATH.
:pt.:pk.*END:epk.
:pd.Open source package path is appended to the end of PATH.
:eparml.
:ehelp.


.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSETPROF
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSETPROF'.
Set Up Pase Profile for User (QSHSETPROF) - Help
:p.This CL command is a convenience command to create open source profile files for a 
selected user ID in their home directory from template source files in QSHONI/SOURCE:
:p.
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPROFILE generates .profile
QSHBASHPRF generates .bash_profile
QSHBASHRC generates .bashrc
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.The following example creates the QShell/PASE .profile, .bashrc and .bash_rc files for the USER1 user ID.
:p.
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSETPROF USER(USER1)     
          PROFILE(*YES)   
          BASHPROFIL(*YES)
          BASHRC(*YES)    
          REPLACE(*NO)   
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.The following example creates or replaces the QShell/PASE .profile, .bashrc and .bash_rc files for the
USER1 user ID.
:p.
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSETPROF USER(USER1)     
          PROFILE(*YES)   
          BASHPROFIL(*YES)
          BASHRC(*YES)    
          REPLACE(*YES)   
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSETPROF/USER'.
User profile (USER) - Help
:xh3.User profile (USER)
:p.Specifies the user profile the PASE profile files are created for. The files are created in the home
directory of the user.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.user-name:epv.
:pd.Enter the user profile name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSETPROF/PROFILE'.
Create .profile for user (PROFILE) - Help
:xh3.Create .profile for user (PROFILE)
:p.Specifies whether the .profile file is created for the user from the QSHPROFILE template source.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The .profile file is created.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The .profile file is not created.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSETPROF/BASHPROFIL'.
Create .bash_profile for user (BASHPROFIL) - Help
:xh3.Create .bash_profile for user (BASHPROFIL)
:p.Specifies whether the .bash_profile file is created for the user from the QSHBASHPRF template source.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The .bash_profile file is created.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The .bash_profile file is not created.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSETPROF/BASHRC'.
Create .bashrc for user (BASHRC) - Help
:xh3.Create .bashrc for user (BASHRC)
:p.Specifies whether the .bashrc file is created for the user from the QSHBASHRC template source.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The .bashrc file is created.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The .bashrc file is not created.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSETPROF/REPLACE'.
Replace if found (REPLACE) - Help
:xh3.Replace if found (REPLACE)
:p.Specifies whether an existing .profile, .bash_profile or .bashrc file is replaced.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Existing files are not replaced.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Existing files are replaced.
:eparml.
:ehelp.




.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSAVLIB
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSAVLIB'.
Save Library to IFS File (QSHSAVLIB) - Help
:p.The Save Library to IFS File (QSHSAVLIB) command saves a library to a temporary save file in QTEMP
using the SAVLIB command and then copies the result to a save file stored in the IFS. The IFS file
can be moved or backed up to a NAS, SAN or other system and later restored with the QSHRSTLIB command.
:p.When *DATETIME or *DATE is used for the TOIFSFILE parameter, the IFS file name is generated in the
directory stored in data area QSHONI/SAVFDIR (default /tmp/savfqsh):
:XMP.
:hp2.
*DATETIME  library_yyyymmdd_hhmmss.savf
*DATE      library_yyyymmdd.savf
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves library MYLIB to IFS file /backups/mylib.savf and replaces the file if it
exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVLIB LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE('/backups/mylib.savf')
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves library MYLIB to an automatically named file in the default save directory
and uses ZLIB compression:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVLIB LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE(*DATETIME)
          DTACPR(*ZLIB)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSAVLIB/LIBRARY'.
Library to save (LIBRARY) - Help
:xh3.Library to save (LIBRARY)
:p.Specifies the library to save.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the library to save.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/TOIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TOIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/REPLACE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REPLACESAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/TGTRLS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TGTRLS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/UPDHST'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/UPDHST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/PRECHK'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRECHK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/SAVACT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVACT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/SAVFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/SPLFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SPLFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/QDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/QDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/DTACPR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DTACPR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVLIB/PROMPT'.
Prompt the SAVLIB command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the SAVLIB command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SAVLIB command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the SAVLIB parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The SAVLIB command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The SAVLIB command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSAVIFS
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSAVIFS'.
Save IFS Objects to IFS File (QSHSAVIFS) - Help
:p.The Save IFS Objects to IFS File (QSHSAVIFS) command saves IFS objects to a temporary save file in QTEMP
using the SAV command and then copies the result to a save file stored in the IFS. The IFS file
can be moved or backed up to a NAS, SAN or other system and later restored with the QSHRSTIFS command.
:p.When *DATETIME or *DATE is used for the TOIFSFILE parameter, the IFS file name is generated in the
directory stored in data area QSHONI/SAVFDIR (default /tmp/savfqsh) using the SAVFPREFIX value:
:XMP.
:hp2.
*DATETIME  savfprefix_yyyymmdd_hhmmss.savf
*DATE      savfprefix_yyyymmdd.savf
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves directory /home/myuser and everything below it to IFS file
/backups/myuser.savf:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVIFS OBJECTS('/home/myuser')
          TOIFSFILE('/backups/myuser.savf')
          SUBTREE(*ALL)
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves directory /home/myuser to an automatically named file that starts with
MYUSER:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVIFS OBJECTS('/home/myuser')
          TOIFSFILE(*DATETIME)
          SAVFPREFIX(MYUSER)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSAVIFS/OBJECTS'.
Objects to save (OBJECTS) - Help
:xh3.Objects to save (OBJECTS)
:p.Specifies the IFS object or directory path to save.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the directory or object to save. The path can be up to 255 characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/TOIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TOIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/SAVFPREFIX'.
Output file keyword prefix (SAVFPREFIX) - Help
:xh3.Output file keyword prefix (SAVFPREFIX)
:p.Specifies the text used at the start of the generated file name when TOIFSFILE is *DATETIME or *DATE.
The value is ignored if you enter your own IFS file name.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.IFSOBJECTS:epk.
:pd.The generated file name starts with IFSOBJECTS.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the prefix to use for the generated file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/SUBTREE'.
Directory subtree (SUBTREE) - Help
:xh3.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:p.Specifies whether the directory subtrees are included in the save operation.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ALL:epk.
:pd.The entire subtree of each directory that matches the object name is saved.
:pt.:pk.*DIR:epk.
:pd.The objects in the first level of each matching directory are saved.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.Only the objects that match the object name are saved. If the object is a directory, its contents are
not
saved.
:pt.:pk.*OBJ:epk.
:pd.Only the matching objects, or the objects in the matching directories, are saved.
:pt.:pk.*STG:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved and their data is saved in a way that keeps the storage reserved for them.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/REPLACE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REPLACESAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/TGTRLS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TGTRLS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/UPDHST'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/UPDHST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/PRECHK'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRECHK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/SAVACT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVACT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/DTACPR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DTACPR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVIFS/PROMPT'.
Prompt the SAV command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the SAV command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SAV command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the SAV parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The SAV command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The SAV command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSAVOBJ
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ'.
Save Objects to IFS File (QSHSAVOBJ) - Help
:p.The Save Objects to IFS File (QSHSAVOBJ) command saves objects from a library to a temporary save file in
QTEMP
using the SAVOBJ command and then copies the result to a save file stored in the IFS. The IFS file
can be moved or backed up to a NAS, SAN or other system and later restored with the QSHRSTOBJ command.
:p.When *DATETIME or *DATE is used for the TOIFSFILE parameter, the IFS file name is generated in the
directory stored in data area QSHONI/SAVFDIR (default /tmp/savfqsh):
:XMP.
:hp2.
*DATETIME  library_SAVOBJ_yyyymmdd_hhmmss.savf
*DATE      library_SAVOBJ_library_yyyymmdd.savf
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves all objects in library MYLIB to IFS file /backups/mylib_objs.savf:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVOBJ OBJECTS(*ALL)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE('/backups/mylib_objs.savf')
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves all objects whose name starts with CUST in library MYLIB to an automatically
named file:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVOBJ OBJECTS(CUST*)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE(*DATETIME)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/OBJECTS'.
Objects to save (OBJECTS) - Help
:xh3.Objects to save (OBJECTS)
:p.Specifies the objects to save from the library.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All of the objects in the library are saved.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the object to save. A generic name (for example CUST*) can be used to save all
objects that start with the same characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/LIBRARY'.
Library to save (LIBRARY) - Help
:xh3.Library to save (LIBRARY)
:p.Specifies the library that contains the objects to save.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the library.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/TOIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TOIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/REPLACE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REPLACESAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/TGTRLS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TGTRLS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/UPDHST'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/UPDHST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/PRECHK'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRECHK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/SAVACT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVACT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/SAVFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/SPLFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SPLFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/QDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/QDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/DTACPR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DTACPR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVOBJ/PROMPT'.
Prompt the SAVLIB command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the SAVLIB command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SAVOBJ command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the SAVOBJ parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The SAVOBJ command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The SAVOBJ command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSAVCHG
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSAVCHG'.
Save Changed Objects to IFS (QSHSAVCHG) - Help
:p.The Save Changed Objects to IFS (QSHSAVCHG) command saves only the objects in a library that have changed
since the last save to a temporary save file in QTEMP
using the SAVCHGOBJ command and then copies the result to a save file stored in the IFS. The IFS file
can be moved or backed up to a NAS, SAN or other system and later restored with the QSHRSTOBJ command.
:p.When *DATETIME or *DATE is used for the TOIFSFILE parameter, the IFS file name is generated in the
directory stored in data area QSHONI/SAVFDIR (default /tmp/savfqsh):
:XMP.
:hp2.
*DATETIME  library_SAVCHGOBJ_yyyymmdd_hhmmss.savf
*DATE      library_SAVCHGOBJ_library_yyyymmdd.savf
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves all objects in library MYLIB that have changed since the last save to IFS
file
/backups/mylib_chg.savf:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVCHG OBJECTS(*ALL)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE('/backups/mylib_chg.savf')
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example saves the changed objects whose name starts with CUST in library MYLIB to an
automatically named file:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSAVCHG OBJECTS(CUST*)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          TOIFSFILE(*DATETIME)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSAVCHG/OBJECTS'.
Objects to save (OBJECTS) - Help
:xh3.Objects to save (OBJECTS)
:p.Specifies the objects to check for changes and save from the library.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All of the objects in the library that have changed are saved.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the object to save. A generic name (for example CUST*) can be used to save all
objects that start with the same characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/LIBRARY'.
Library to save (LIBRARY) - Help
:xh3.Library to save (LIBRARY)
:p.Specifies the library that contains the objects to save.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the library.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/TOIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TOIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/REPLACE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REPLACESAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/TGTRLS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/TGTRLS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/UPDHST'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/UPDHST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/PRECHK'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRECHK'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/SAVACT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVACT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/SAVFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SAVFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/SPLFDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SPLFDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/QDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/QDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/DTACPR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DTACPR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSAVCHG/PROMPT'.
Prompt the SAVCHGOBJ command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the SAVCHGOBJ command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SAVCHGOBJ command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for
testing
or reviewing the SAVCHGOBJ parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The SAVCHGOBJ command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The SAVCHGOBJ command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHRSTLIB
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHRSTLIB'.
Restore Library from IFS File (QSHRSTLIB) - Help
:p.The Restore Library from IFS File (QSHRSTLIB) command copies a save file stored in the IFS to a temporary
save file in QTEMP and then restores a library from it using the RSTLIB command. The IFS file is normally
one created by the QSHSAVLIB command.
:p.The following example restores library MYLIB from IFS file /backups/mylib.savf back into library MYLIB:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHRSTLIB LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          FRMIFSFILE('/backups/mylib.savf')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example restores the library that was saved as MYLIB into library MYLIBTST. Library
MYLIBTST
is cleared first if it already exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHRSTLIB LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          RSTLIB(MYLIBTST)
          CLRLIB(*YES)
          FRMIFSFILE('/backups/mylib.savf')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHRSTLIB/LIBRARY'.
Library to restore (LIBRARY) - Help
:xh3.Library to restore (LIBRARY)
:p.Specifies the name of the library as it was saved in the save file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the saved library to restore.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/RSTLIB'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/RSTLIB'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/CLRLIB'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CLRLIB'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/FRMIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/FRMIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/OPTION'.
Option (OPTION) - Help
:xh3.Option (OPTION)
:p.Specifies which objects are restored.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. This parameter is only used when PROMPT(*YES) is specified. When PROMPT(*NO) is used
the command restores with OPTION(*ALL).
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All objects in the save file are restored, whether or not they already exist in the library.
:pt.:pk.*NEW:epk.
:pd.Only objects that do not already exist in the library are restored.
:pt.:pk.*OLD:epk.
:pd.Only objects that already exist in the library are restored.
:pt.:pk.*FREE:epk.
:pd.Only objects whose storage was freed when they were saved are restored.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/MBROPT'.
Database member option (MBROPT) - Help
:xh3.Database member option (MBROPT)
:p.Specifies which database file members are restored.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. This parameter is only used when PROMPT(*YES) is specified. When PROMPT(*NO) is used
the command restores with MBROPT(*ALL).
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All members in the save file are restored.
:pt.:pk.*NEW:epk.
:pd.Only members that do not already exist in the file are restored.
:pt.:pk.*OLD:epk.
:pd.Only members that already exist in the file are restored.
:pt.:pk.*MATCH:epk.
:pd.Only members that exist in both the save file and the database file are restored.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/ALWOBJDIF'.
Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF) - Help
:xh3.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:p.Specifies whether differences between the saved objects and the objects on the system are allowed during
the restore.
Differences include such things as owner, authorization list or file level identifiers.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. This parameter is only used when PROMPT(*YES) is specified. When PROMPT(*NO) is used
the command restores with ALWOBJDIF(*ALL).
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All differences are allowed. Objects are restored even if differences are found.
:pt.:pk.*COMPATIBLE:epk.
:pd.Differences are allowed as long as the object can still be used.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No differences are allowed. Objects with differences are not restored.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTLIB/PROMPT'.
Prompt the RSTLIB command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the RSTLIB command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the RSTLIB command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the RSTLIB parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The RSTLIB command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The RSTLIB command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHRSTIFS
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHRSTIFS'.
Restore IFS Obj from IFS File (QSHRSTIFS) - Help
:p.The Restore IFS Obj from IFS File (QSHRSTIFS) command copies a save file stored in the IFS to a temporary
save file in QTEMP and then restores IFS objects from it using the RST command. The IFS file is normally
one created by the QSHSAVIFS command. Objects are restored with their entire subtree and parent directories
are created if needed.
:p.The following example restores directory /home/myuser and everything below it from IFS file
/backups/myuser.savf:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHRSTIFS OBJECTS('/home/myuser')
          FRMIFSFILE('/backups/myuser.savf')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHRSTIFS/OBJECTS'.
IFS objects to restore (OBJECTS) - Help
:xh3.IFS objects to restore (OBJECTS)
:p.Specifies the IFS object or directory path to restore from the save file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the directory or object to restore. The path can be up to 255 characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTIFS/FRMIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/FRMIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTIFS/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTIFS/PROMPT'.
Prompt the RST command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the RST command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the RST command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the RST parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The RST command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The RST command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHRSTOBJ
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ'.
Restore Objects from IFS File (QSHRSTOBJ) - Help
:p.The Restore Objects from IFS File (QSHRSTOBJ) command copies a save file stored in the IFS to a temporary
save file in QTEMP and then restores objects from it using the RSTOBJ command. The IFS file is normally
one created by the QSHSAVOBJ or QSHSAVCHG command.
:p.The following example restores all objects saved from library MYLIB in IFS file /backups/mylib_objs.savf:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHRSTOBJ OBJECTS(*ALL)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          FRMIFSFILE('/backups/mylib_objs.savf')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example restores the objects whose name starts with CUST into library MYLIBTST:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHRSTOBJ OBJECTS(CUST*)
          LIBRARY(MYLIB)
          RSTLIB(MYLIBTST)
          FRMIFSFILE('/backups/mylib_objs.savf')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/OBJECTS'.
Objects to save (OBJECTS) - Help
:xh3.Objects to save (OBJECTS)
:p.Specifies the objects to restore from the save file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All of the objects in the save file are restored.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the object to restore. A generic name (for example CUST*) can be used to restore all
objects that start with the same characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/LIBRARY'.
Library to restore (LIBRARY) - Help
:xh3.Library to restore (LIBRARY)
:p.Specifies the name of the library the objects were saved from, as it is recorded in the save file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the saved library.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/RSTLIB'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/RSTLIB'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/CLRLIB'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CLRLIB'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/FRMIFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/FRMIFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHRSTOBJ/PROMPT'.
Prompt the RSTOBJ command (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the RSTOBJ command (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the RSTOBJ command is prompted interactively before it runs. This is useful for testing
or reviewing the RSTOBJ parameter values. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The RSTOBJ command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The RSTOBJ command is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHVFYSAVF
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHVFYSAVF'.
Verify IFS Save File (QSHVFYSAVF) - Help
:p.The Verify IFS Save File (QSHVFYSAVF) command checks that a save file stored in the IFS is still usable.
It copies the IFS file to a temporary save file in QTEMP and can display or print the contents of the save
file.
If the copy works the command ends with a completion message saying the file appears to be valid.
Use it to check a save file after it was moved or backed up.
:p.The following example verifies IFS file /backups/mylib.savf and displays its contents:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHVFYSAVF FRMIFSSAVF('/backups/mylib.savf')
           DSPSAVF(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHVFYSAVF/FRMIFSSAVF'.
From IFS save file (FRMIFSSAVF) - Help
:xh3.From IFS save file (FRMIFSSAVF)
:p.Specifies the IFS file that contains the save file data to verify.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name of the save file. The command ends with an error if the file is
not
found.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHVFYSAVF/DSPSAVF'.
Display save file (DSPSAVF) - Help
:xh3.Display save file (DSPSAVF)
:p.Specifies whether the contents of the save file are displayed using the Display Save File (DSPSAVF)
command.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The save file contents are not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The save file contents are displayed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHVFYSAVF/PRTSAVF'.
Print save file contents (PRTSAVF) - Help
:xh3.Print save file contents (PRTSAVF)
:p.Specifies whether the contents of the save file are printed. The spooled file is held.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The save file contents are not printed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The save file contents are printed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHVFYSAVF/DLTTMPSAVF'.
Delete temp save file after (DLTTMPSAVF) - Help
:xh3.Delete temp save file after (DLTTMPSAVF)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary save file in library QTEMP is deleted when the command ends.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary save file in QTEMP is not deleted. It can be used for further checks in the same job.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary save file in QTEMP is deleted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSSH
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSSH'.
Run Remote Command over SSH (QSHSSH) - Help
:p.The Run Remote Command over SSH (QSHSSH) command runs a command on a remote IBM i or other system
using the ssh utility and captures the STDOUT results. This is a convenient way to run or submit
a job on a remote system. The command can sign on with an SSH private key or with a user and password.
:p.When a password is used the open source sshpass package must be installed (/QOpenSys/pkgs/bin/sshpass).
A private key is recommended over a password.
:p.The following example runs the ls command on a remote system with an SSH private key and displays the
results:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSSH SSHHOST('myhost.com')
       SSHPORT(22)
       SSHUSER(user1)
       KEYFILE('/home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa')
       CMDLINE('ls -l /tmp')
       DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example runs the same command with a user and password:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSSH SSHHOST('myhost.com')
       SSHUSER(user1)
       SSHPASS('mypassword')
       CMDLINE('ls -l /tmp')
       DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSSH/SSHHOST'.
SFTP server host/ip address (SSHHOST) - Help
:xh3.SFTP server host/ip address (SSHHOST)
:p.Specifies the host name or IP address of the remote system to run the command on.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the host name or IP address of the remote SSH server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/SSHPORT'.
SFTP server port (SSHPORT) - Help
:xh3.SFTP server port (SSHPORT)
:p.Specifies the TCP/IP port number the SSH server on the remote system listens on.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.22:epk.
:pd.The standard SSH port 22 is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the port number the remote SSH server is using.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/SSHUSER'.
SFTP user (SSHUSER) - Help
:xh3.SFTP user (SSHUSER)
:p.Specifies the user name used to sign on to the remote system.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user name on the remote system.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/SSHPASS'.
SFTP password (SSHPASS) - Help
:xh3.SFTP password (SSHPASS)
:p.Specifies the password used to sign on to the remote system. When a password is entered the sshpass
utility is used and the private key file value is ignored. The password is passed on the PASE command line,
so a private key file is recommended instead.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No password is used. The private key file or the default SSH keys of the user are used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the password for the user on the remote system.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/KEYFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SSHKEYFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/KEYPASSWD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/KEYPASSWD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/CMDLINE'.
Command line to run (CMDLINE) - Help
:xh3.Command line to run (CMDLINE)
:p.Specifies the command line to run on the remote system. The command line is enclosed in double quotes
when it is passed to ssh. Semicolons can be used to run multiple commands.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the command line to run on the remote system. The value can be up to 2000 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSSH/PROMPTQSH'.
Prompt for shell command line (PROMPTQSH) - Help
:xh3.Prompt for shell command line (PROMPTQSH)
:p.This option determines if the QSH command is prompted interactively for testing or
review of the actual QShell command line with parameter values before running the command.
Normally the selection should be *NO since prompting is only needed if testing.
Specify *YES if you are debugging for some reason and want the QSH command to prompt
on an interactive 5250 session before running.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Does not prompt the QSH command for testing or review.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Prompts the QSH command for testing or review before running.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSCP
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSCP'.
Run SCP Command via QShell (QSHSCP) - Help
:p.The Run SCP Command via QShell (QSHSCP) command transfers a file or directory between the local IBM i IFS
and a remote system over an SSH connection using the scp utility. It is an alternative to SFTP.
The command signs on with an SSH private key file.
:p.The following example sends a local file to a remote system:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSCP LOCALFILE('/home/user1/mylib.savf')
       REMOTEFILE('/home/user1/mylib.savf')
       KEYFILE('/home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa')
       USER(user1)
       HOST('myhost.com')
       PORT(22)
       ACTION(*SEND)
       DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example receives a remote file and replaces the local file if it exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSCP LOCALFILE('/home/user1/mylib.savf')
       REMOTEFILE('/home/user1/mylib.savf')
       KEYFILE('/home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa')
       USER(user1)
       HOST('myhost.com')
       ACTION(*RECEIVE)
       REPLLOCAL(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSCP/LOCALFILE'.
Local file or directory (LOCALFILE) - Help
:xh3.Local file or directory (LOCALFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS path of the file or directory on the local system. It is the source when
ACTION(*SEND) is used and the destination when ACTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the local file or directory.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/REMOTEFILE'.
Remote file or directory (REMOTEFILE) - Help
:xh3.Remote file or directory (REMOTEFILE)
:p.Specifies the path of the file or directory on the remote system. It is the destination when
ACTION(*SEND) is used and the source when ACTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the path of the remote file or directory.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/KEYFILE'.
SSH private key file (KEYFILE) - Help
:xh3.SSH private key file (KEYFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS path of the SSH private key file used to sign on to the remote system.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the private key file. For example /home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/USER'.
User name (USER) - Help
:xh3.User name (USER)
:p.Specifies the user name used to sign on to the remote system.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user name on the remote system.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/HOST'.
Host name (HOST) - Help
:xh3.Host name (HOST)
:p.Specifies the host name or IP address of the remote system.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the host name or IP address of the remote system.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/CMDPFXPARM'.
Scp command prefix parms (CMDPFXPARM) - Help
:xh3.Scp command prefix parms (CMDPFXPARM)
:p.Specifies extra options that are placed on the scp command line before the other parameters.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No extra options are passed to scp.
:pt.:pk.*VERBOSE:epk.
:pd.Passes -v to show verbose output.
:pt.:pk.*COMPRESS:epk.
:pd.Passes -C to compress the data during transfer.
:pt.:pk.*VERBOSECOMPRESS:epk.
:pd.Passes -v -C.
:pt.:pk.*RECURSE:epk.
:pd.Passes -r to copy directories recursively.
:pt.:pk.*RECURSEVERBOSE:epk.
:pd.Passes -r -v.
:pt.:pk.*RECURSEVERBOSECOMPRESS:epk.
:pd.Passes -r -v -C.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter any scp options. The value can be up to 1000 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PORT'.
TCP port (PORT) - Help
:xh3.TCP port (PORT)
:p.Specifies the TCP/IP port number the SSH server on the remote system listens on.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.22:epk.
:pd.The standard SSH port 22 is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the port number the remote SSH server is using.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/ACTION'.
Transfer action (ACTION) - Help
:xh3.Transfer action (ACTION)
:p.Specifies the direction of the transfer.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SEND:epk.
:pd.The local file or directory is sent to the remote system.
:pt.:pk.*RECEIVE:epk.
:pd.The remote file or directory is received into the local system.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/FILEOPT'.
Sending file or directory (FILEOPT) - Help
:xh3.Sending file or directory (FILEOPT)
:p.Specifies whether the local object is a single file or a directory. The command checks that a local
file exists before sending when *FILE is used. Use *DIR together with the *RECURSE
option of CMDPFXPARM to copy a directory.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*FILE:epk.
:pd.The transfer is for a single file.
:pt.:pk.*DIR:epk.
:pd.The transfer is for a directory.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/REPLLOCAL'.
Replace local file on receive (REPLLOCAL) - Help
:xh3.Replace local file on receive (REPLLOCAL)
:p.Specifies whether an existing local file is replaced when ACTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.If the local file already exists the command ends with an error and nothing is received.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the local file already exists it is replaced by the received file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/DEBUGCMD'.
Debug PASE command line (DEBUGCMD) - Help
:xh3.Debug PASE command line (DEBUGCMD)
:p.Specifies whether the scp command line is prompted before it runs so you can review the command line
that is passed to the PASE shell. This is useful for testing. Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The scp command line is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The scp command line is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSCP/PASEJOBNAM'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PASEJOBNAM'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHLFTP
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHLFTP'.
Send/Rcv Files via Lftp/Sftp (QSHLFTP) - Help
:p.The Send/Rcv Files via Lftp/Sftp (QSHLFTP) command uploads or downloads a file using the SFTP
support in the open source lftp utility. The lftp package must be installed (/QOpenSys/pkgs/bin/lftp).
The command signs on with a user and password or with an SSH private key file.
:p.The following example uploads a local file to an SFTP server with an SSH private key:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHLFTP SFTPHOST('sftp.myhost.com')
        SFTPPORT(22)
        SFTPUSER(user1)
        KEYFILE('/home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa')
        LOCALFILE('/home/user1/mylib.savf')
        REMOTEFILE('/uploads/mylib.savf')
        OPTION(*SEND)
        DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example downloads a file from an SFTP server with a user and password and replaces
the local file if it exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHLFTP SFTPHOST('sftp.myhost.com')
        SFTPUSER(user1)
        SFTPPASS('mypassword')
        LOCALFILE('/tmp/report.csv')
        REMOTEFILE('/downloads/report.csv')
        OPTION(*RECEIVE)
        REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHLFTP/SFTPHOST'.
SFTP server host/ip address (SFTPHOST) - Help
:xh3.SFTP server host/ip address (SFTPHOST)
:p.Specifies the host name or IP address of the SFTP server.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the host name or IP address of the SFTP server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/SFTPPORT'.
SFTP server port (SFTPPORT) - Help
:xh3.SFTP server port (SFTPPORT)
:p.Specifies the TCP/IP port number the SSH server on the remote system listens on.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.22:epk.
:pd.The standard SSH port 22 is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the port number the remote SSH server is using.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/SFTPUSER'.
SFTP user (SFTPUSER) - Help
:xh3.SFTP user (SFTPUSER)
:p.Specifies the user name used to sign on to the SFTP server.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user name on the SFTP server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/SFTPPASS'.
SFTP password (SFTPPASS) - Help
:xh3.SFTP password (SFTPPASS)
:p.Specifies the password used to sign on to the SFTP server. The password is passed on the PASE command
line,
so a private key file is recommended instead.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No password is used. Use this with a private key file.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the password for the user on the SFTP server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/KEYFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SSHKEYFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/KEYPASSWD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/KEYPASSWD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/LOCALFILE'.
Local file (LOCALFILE) - Help
:xh3.Local file (LOCALFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS path of the file on the local system. It is the source when OPTION(*SEND) is used
and the destination when OPTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the local file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/REMOTEFILE'.
Remote file (REMOTEFILE) - Help
:xh3.Remote file (REMOTEFILE)
:p.Specifies the path of the file on the SFTP server. It is the destination when OPTION(*SEND) is used
and the source when OPTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the path and file name on the SFTP server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/OPTION'.
Transfer option (OPTION) - Help
:xh3.Transfer option (OPTION)
:p.Specifies the direction of the transfer.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SEND:epk.
:pd.The local file is uploaded to the SFTP server.
:pt.:pk.*RECEIVE:epk.
:pd.The remote file is downloaded from the SFTP server.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/REPLACE'.
Replace destination file (REPLACE) - Help
:xh3.Replace destination file (REPLACE)
:p.Specifies whether an existing local file is replaced when OPTION(*RECEIVE) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the local file already exists it is replaced by the downloaded file.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.If the local file already exists the command ends with an error and nothing is downloaded.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHLFTP/PROMPTQSH'.
Prompt for shell command line (PROMPTQSH) - Help
:xh3.Prompt for shell command line (PROMPTQSH)
:p.This option determines if the QSH command is prompted interactively for testing or
review of the actual QShell command line with parameter values before running the command.
Normally the selection should be *NO since prompting is only needed if testing.
Specify *YES if you are debugging for some reason and want the QSH command to prompt
on an interactive 5250 session before running.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Does not prompt the QSH command for testing or review.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Prompts the QSH command for testing or review before running.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPORTCHK
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPORTCHK'.
Check for Active TCP/IP Port (QSHPORTCHK) - Help
:p.The Check for Active TCP/IP Port (QSHPORTCHK) command uses Db2 for i services to check whether the
selected TCP/IP port has an application running on it. The command completes successfully if the port is
active. If the port is not active a CPF9898 escape message is sent. This makes the command useful in a
CL program to test whether a server is running.
:p.The following example checks whether a Postgres server instance is running on port 5432:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPORTCHK LOCALPORT(5432)
           CONNTYPE(IPV4)
           OUTFILE(QTEMP/TCPTMP001)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHPORTCHK/LOCALPORT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOCALPORT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPORTCHK/CONNTYPE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CONNTYPE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPORTCHK/OUTFILE'.
Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the temporary file that receives the port information found. The file is created
in the job's QTEMP library by default.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.TCPTMP001:epk.
:pd.The results are written to file TCPTMP001.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file to receive the results.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The file is created in library QTEMP.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library for the file.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPORTEND
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPORTEND'.
End Jobs for Active TCP Port (QSHPORTEND) - Help
:p.The End Jobs for Active TCP Port (QSHPORTEND) command uses Db2 for i services to find the jobs that
are using the selected TCP/IP port and ends them. The command completes successfully whether or not the
port was active and sends a message showing the number of jobs that were ended.
:p.The following example ends all jobs using port 443:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPORTEND LOCALPORT(443)
           CONNTYPE(IPV4)
           OUTFILE(QTEMP/TCPTMPEND)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHPORTEND/LOCALPORT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOCALPORT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPORTEND/CONNTYPE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CONNTYPE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPORTEND/OUTFILE'.
Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the temporary file that receives the list of jobs found on the port. The file is created
in the job's QTEMP library by default.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.TCPTMPEND:epk.
:pd.The results are written to file TCPTMPEND.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file to receive the results.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The file is created in library QTEMP.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library for the file.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHENDWEB
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHENDWEB'.
End Web Server (QSHENDWEB) - Help
:p.The End Web Server (QSHENDWEB) command ends an HTTP server instance with the End TCP/IP Server
(ENDTCPSVR) command and then monitors the active jobs to make sure the server jobs end. The command
checks for the jobs every DLYJOB seconds, up to WAITCYCLES times. If the jobs have not ended after that
time a message is sent saying the instance may not have ended.
:p.The following example ends HTTP server instance MYWEB and waits up to 10 cycles of 10 seconds each
for the jobs to end:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHENDWEB HTTPINST(MYWEB)
          JOBNAME(*HTTPINST)
          DLYJOB(10)
          WAITCYCLES(10)
          SNDOPRMSG(*YES)
          TOUSR(*SYSOPR)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHENDWEB/HTTPINST'.
HTTP instance name (HTTPINST) - Help
:xh3.HTTP instance name (HTTPINST)
:p.Specifies the name of the HTTP server instance to end.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the HTTP server instance name.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHENDWEB/JOBNAME'.
Job name (JOBNAME) - Help
:xh3.Job name (JOBNAME)
:p.Specifies the job name that is monitored to determine when the server has ended. The name can be
generic, for example ADMIN* for the *ADMIN instance jobs. For most HTTP server instances the job name
is the same as the instance name.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*HTTPINST:epk.
:pd.The HTTP instance name is used as the job name.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the job name to monitor.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHENDWEB/DLYJOB'.
Delay job in seconds (DLYJOB) - Help
:xh3.Delay job in seconds (DLYJOB)
:p.Specifies the number of seconds to wait between each check for active server jobs.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.10:epk.
:pd.The command waits 10 seconds between checks.
:pt.:pv.number:epv.
:pd.Enter the number of seconds to wait.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHENDWEB/WAITCYCLES'.
Number of delay cycles to wait (WAITCYCLES) - Help
:xh3.Number of delay cycles to wait (WAITCYCLES)
:p.Specifies how many times the command checks for active server jobs before it gives up. The total wait
time is about DLYJOB multiplied by WAITCYCLES seconds.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.10:epk.
:pd.The command checks up to 10 times.
:pt.:pv.number:epv.
:pd.Enter the number of times to check.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHENDWEB/SNDOPRMSG'.
Send operator message (SNDOPRMSG) - Help
:xh3.Send operator message (SNDOPRMSG)
:p.Specifies whether an informational message is sent to a user about the result of ending the server.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.No message is sent.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.A message is sent to the user in the TOUSR parameter when the instance is not running,
ended successfully or may not have ended.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHENDWEB/TOUSR'.
To user (TOUSR) - Help
:xh3.To user (TOUSR)
:p.Specifies the user or message queue that receives the message when SNDOPRMSG(*YES) is used.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SYSOPR:epk.
:pd.The message is sent to the system operator.
:pt.:pv.user-name:epv.
:pd.Enter the user profile name to send the message to.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHIFSCHK
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHIFSCHK'.
Check for IFS File/Dir Exist (QSHIFSCHK) - Help
:p.The Check for IFS File/Dir Exist (QSHIFSCHK) command checks whether an IFS file or directory exists.
The command always ends with an escape message, so the result is tested in a CL program with the
Monitor Message (MONMSG) command:
:XMP.
:hp2.
CPF9897  The file or directory was found.
CPF9898  The file or directory was not found.
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example checks for a file and runs different logic depending on whether it was found:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHIFSCHK FILNAM('/tmp/myfile.txt')
MONMSG MSGID(CPF9897) EXEC(DO)
   /* File exists */
ENDDO
MONMSG MSGID(CPF9898) EXEC(DO)
   /* File does not exist */
ENDDO
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHIFSCHK/FILNAM'.
IFS file or directory name (FILNAM) - Help
:xh3.IFS file or directory name (FILNAM)
:p.Specifies the IFS file or directory to check for.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the file or directory. The value can be up to 255 characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHIFSSCAN
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHIFSSCAN'.
Scan IFS File for Value (QSHIFSSCAN) - Help
:p.The Scan IFS File for Value (QSHIFSSCAN) command scans an IFS text file for one or more values. The main
use is to scan a STDOUT or STDERR log file for text that shows success or failure. The command ends
successfully as soon as any one of the values is found. If none of the values are found, or the IFS file
does not exist, a CPF9898 escape message is sent that can be monitored in a CL program.
:p.The following example checks whether the word :hp3.successfully:ehp3. appears anywhere on a line of a log
file:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHIFSSCAN IFSFILE('/tmp/job.log')
           SCANFOR('successfully')
           EXACTMATCH(*NO)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example scans for either of two values and monitors for the not found message:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHIFSSCAN IFSFILE('/tmp/job.log')
           SCANFOR('Build complete' 'Build succeeded')
MONMSG MSGID(CPF9898) EXEC(DO)
   /* Neither value was found */
ENDDO
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHIFSSCAN/IFSFILE'.
IFS file to scan (IFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.IFS file to scan (IFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS text file to scan.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the file to scan. The command ends with an error if the file does not exist.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSCAN/SCANFOR'.
Values to scan for first match (SCANFOR) - Help
:xh3.Values to scan for first match (SCANFOR)
:p.Specifies the text values to scan for on each line of the file.
The values are case sensitive and must match the text in the file. The scan ends as soon as any one of the
values is found.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the value to scan for. Up to 20 values of up to 100 characters each can be entered.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LIST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSCAN/EXACTMATCH'.
Exact match-*YES, Contains-*NO (EXACTMATCH) - Help
:xh3.Exact match-*YES, Contains-*NO (EXACTMATCH)
:p.Specifies how a value must match a line in the file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.At least one line must contain the value somewhere in the line. Good for generic matching.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The value must match exactly and be the only thing on the line.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSCAN/ENDLINFMT'.
End of line characters (ENDLINFMT) - Help
:xh3.End of line characters (ENDLINFMT)
:p.Specifies the characters that mark the end of each line in the IFS file. This is used when the file is
copied to a temporary physical file in QTEMP before it is scanned.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ALL:epk.
:pd.Any combination of carriage return and line feed characters ends a line.
:pt.:pk.*CR:epk.
:pd.A carriage return ends a line.
:pt.:pk.*LF:epk.
:pd.A line feed ends a line.
:pt.:pk.*CRLF:epk.
:pd.A carriage return followed by a line feed ends a line.
:pt.:pk.*LFCR:epk.
:pd.A line feed followed by a carriage return ends a line.
:pt.:pk.*FIXED:epk.
:pd.The file has fixed length lines with no end of line characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSCAN/DLTTMPFILE'.
Delete temp file after (DLTTMPFILE) - Help
:xh3.Delete temp file after (DLTTMPFILE)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary file TMPIFSFILE in library QTEMP is deleted after the scan.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary file is deleted.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary file is not deleted. It can be used for testing or review in the same job.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHIFSSIZ
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHIFSSIZ'.
Retrieve IFS Object Size (QSHIFSSIZ) - Help
:p.The Retrieve IFS Object Size (QSHIFSSIZ) command returns the size and the allocated size of an IFS
file in bytes. The values are returned in CL variables, so the command must be run from a CL program.
:p.The following example retrieves the size of a file into CL variables:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DCL VAR(&amp.SIZE) TYPE(*DEC) LEN(15 0)
DCL VAR(&amp.ALLOCSIZE) TYPE(*DEC) LEN(15 0)
QSHIFSSIZ FILE('/tmp/myfile.txt')
          SIZE(&amp.SIZE)
          ALLOCSIZE(&amp.ALLOCSIZE)
          ESCONERROR(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHIFSSIZ/FILE'.
IFS file name (FILE) - Help
:xh3.IFS file name (FILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file to retrieve the size of.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.path-name:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSIZ/SIZE'.
Return file size (15 0) (SIZE) - Help
:xh3.Return file size (15 0) (SIZE)
:p.Specifies the CL variable that receives the size of the IFS file in bytes.
The variable must be a decimal variable with a length of 15 and 0 decimal positions.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.decimal-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the CL variable to receive the file size.
If the file is not found and ESCONERROR(*NO) is used, the value -2 is returned.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSIZ/ALLOCSIZE'.
Return allocated size (15 0) (ALLOCSIZE) - Help
:xh3.Return allocated size (15 0) (ALLOCSIZE)
:p.Specifies the CL variable that receives the allocated size of the IFS file in bytes. The allocated size
is the storage the file uses on disk. The variable must be a decimal variable with a length of 15 and
0 decimal positions.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.decimal-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the CL variable to receive the allocated size.
If the file is not found and ESCONERROR(*NO) is used, the value -2 is returned.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHIFSSIZ/ESCONERROR'.
Escape error on not found (ESCONERROR) - Help
:xh3.Escape error on not found (ESCONERROR)
:p.Specifies whether an escape message is sent when the IFS file cannot be found.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.A CPF9898 escape message is sent if the file is not found.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.No escape message is sent. The size values are set to -2 and a diagnostic message is sent.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHHOME
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHHOME'.
Retrieve Home Dir (QSHHOME) - Help
:p.The Retrieve Home Dir (QSHHOME) command returns the IFS home directory of the user profile the job
is running under. The value is returned in a CL variable, so the command must be run from a CL program.
If the home directory cannot be determined the variable is set to blanks.
:p.The following example retrieves the home directory:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DCL VAR(&amp.HOMEDIR) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(640)
QSHHOME HOMEDIR(&amp.HOMEDIR)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHHOME/HOMEDIR'.
Return home dir (HOMEDIR) - Help
:xh3.Return home dir (HOMEDIR)
:p.Specifies the CL variable that receives the home directory path.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of a character CL variable with a length of 640.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHCPYSRC
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHCPYSRC'.
Copy Source Member to Script (QSHCPYSRC) - Help
:p.The Copy Source Member to Script (QSHCPYSRC) command copies a source member to an IFS script file
so that it can be run with Qshell, PASE or bash. When TOIFSFILE(*GENERATE) is used the file is created in
directory /tmp/qsh with a name made up of the member name, the date and time, the user name, and the
source type of the member as the extension.
:p.The following example copies member MYSCRIPT in source file QSHONI/QSHSCRIPTS to an automatically named
script file:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHCPYSRC SRCFILE(QSHONI/QSHSCRIPTS)
          SRCMBR(MYSCRIPT)
          TOIFSFILE(*GENERATE)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example copies the member to a specific IFS file and replaces the file if it exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHCPYSRC SRCFILE(QSHONI/QSHSCRIPTS)
          SRCMBR(MYSCRIPT)
          TOIFSFILE('/home/user1/myscript.sh')
          IFSOPT(*REPLACE)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHCPYSRC/SRCFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCPYSRC/SRCMBR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCMBR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCPYSRC/SRCTYPE'.
Source type for auto generate (SRCTYPE) - Help
:xh3.Source type for auto generate (SRCTYPE)
:p.Specifies the file extension used when the IFS file name is generated with TOIFSFILE(*GENERATE).
The value is ignored if you enter your own IFS file name.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*MEMBER:epk.
:pd.The source type of the source member is used as the file extension.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the file extension to use, for example sh or py.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCPYSRC/TOIFSFILE'.
To IFS script file (TOIFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.To IFS script file (TOIFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file the source member is copied to.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*GENERATE:epk.
:pd.The file name is generated in directory /tmp/qsh.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name of the script file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCPYSRC/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHSRCIFS
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHSRCIFS'.
Copy Source Mbr to IFS File (QSHSRCIFS) - Help
:p.The Copy Source Mbr to IFS File (QSHSRCIFS) command copies a source member to an IFS file. When
IFSFILE(*GENERATE) is used the file is created in directory /tmp/qsh with a name made up of the member
name, the date and time, the user name and the extension .sh.
:p.The following example copies member MYSCRIPT in source file QSHONI/QSHSCRIPTS to an IFS file and
replaces the file if it exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHSRCIFS SRCFILE(QSHONI/QSHSCRIPTS)
          SRCMBR(MYSCRIPT)
          IFSFILE('/home/user1/myscript.sh')
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHSRCIFS/SRCFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSRCIFS/SRCMBR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCMBR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSRCIFS/IFSFILE'.
Destination IFS file (IFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.Destination IFS file (IFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file the source member is copied to.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*GENERATE:epk.
:pd.The file name is generated in directory /tmp/qsh.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHSRCIFS/REPLACE'.
Replace existing IFS file (REPLACE) - Help
:xh3.Replace existing IFS file (REPLACE)
:p.Specifies whether an existing IFS file is replaced.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.If the IFS file already exists the command ends with an error and nothing is copied.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the IFS file already exists it is replaced.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHWRTLOG
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHWRTLOG'.
Write Simple Log Message (QSHWRTLOG) - Help
:p.The Write Simple Log Message (QSHWRTLOG) command writes a message to a simple log file. This lets an
application keep its own log instead of relying on the job log for all messages. The log file is
created automatically if it does not exist. The log can be printed later with the QSHPRTLOG command.
:p.The following example writes an informational message to log file QTEMP/LOGTMP0001:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHWRTLOG MSG('This is a sample message')
          MSGTYPE(INFO)
          LOGFILE(QTEMP/LOGTMP0001)
          RECREATE(*NO)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.Set RECREATE(*YES) on the first call in a job to clear the log, and use RECREATE(*NO) on later calls so
the
log records accumulate.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHWRTLOG/MSG'.
Message (MSG) - Help
:xh3.Message (MSG)
:p.Specifies the message text to write to the log file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the message text. The text can be up to 330 characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHWRTLOG/MSGTYPE'.
Message type (MSGTYPE) - Help
:xh3.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:p.Specifies the type that is stored with the message in the log file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.INFO:epk.
:pd.The message is an informational message.
:pt.:pk.WARNING:epk.
:pd.The message is a warning.
:pt.:pk.ERROR:epk.
:pd.The message is an error.
:pt.:pk.DIAG:epk.
:pd.The message is a diagnostic message.
:pt.:pk.COMP:epk.
:pd.The message is a completion message.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter your own message type of up to 10 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHWRTLOG/LOGFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHWRTLOG/RECREATE'.
Dlt and create log file before (RECREATE) - Help
:xh3.Dlt and create log file before (RECREATE)
:p.Specifies whether the log file is deleted and created again before the message is written.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The log file is created if it does not exist. If it exists the message is added to it.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The log file is deleted if it exists and then created again, so it only holds the new message.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPRTLOG
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPRTLOG'.
Print Simple Log File (QSHPRTLOG) - Help
:p.The Print Simple Log File (QSHPRTLOG) command prints a simple log file that was written by the QSHWRTLOG
command. The log is printed to a spool file with a width of 378 characters, or it can be written to a
PDF file in the IFS.
:p.The following example prints log file QTEMP/LOGTMP0001 to a spool file named PRTLOG:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPRTLOG LOGFILE(QTEMP/LOGTMP0001)
          PRTSPLF(PRTLOG)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example creates a PDF of the log in the IFS and replaces the PDF if it exists:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPRTLOG LOGFILE(QTEMP/LOGTMP0001)
          IFSFILE('/tmp/mylog.pdf')
          REPLACE(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHPRTLOG/LOGFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/IFSFILE'.
IFS PDF output file name (IFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.IFS PDF output file name (IFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file that receives a PDF version of the log.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No PDF is created. The log is printed to a spool file.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name of the PDF file to create.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/REPLACE'.
Replace existing PDF if found (REPLACE) - Help
:xh3.Replace existing PDF if found (REPLACE)
:p.Specifies whether an existing PDF file is replaced. This is only used when an IFS file name is entered.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.If the PDF file already exists the command ends with an error and nothing is created.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the PDF file already exists it is deleted and created again.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/PRTSPLF'.
Print spool file (PRTSPLF) - Help
:xh3.Print spool file (PRTSPLF)
:p.Specifies the name of the spool file that is created.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.PRTLOG:epk.
:pd.The spool file is named PRTLOG.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the spool file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/PRTUSRDTA'.
Print user data (PRTUSRDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print user data (PRTUSRDTA)
:p.Specifies the user data that is stored with the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No user data is stored.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user data of up to 10 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/PRTTXT'.
Print print text (PRTTXT) - Help
:xh3.Print print text (PRTTXT)
:p.Specifies the print text that is shown at the bottom of each page of the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No print text is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the print text of up to 30 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/PRTHOLD'.
Print hold spool file (PRTHOLD) - Help
:xh3.Print hold spool file (PRTHOLD)
:p.Specifies whether the spool file is held on the output queue.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The spool file is held.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The spool file is released for printing.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPRTLOG/PRTOUTQ'.
Print to outq (PRTOUTQ) - Help
:xh3.Print to outq (PRTOUTQ)
:p.Specifies the output queue the spool file is placed on.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SAME:epk.
:pd.The spool file is placed on the output queue of the job.
:pt.:pv.output-queue-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the output queue.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the output queue.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the output queue is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHJOBLIST
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHJOBLIST'.
List Selected Jobs to Outfile (QSHJOBLIST) - Help
:p.The List Selected Jobs to Outfile (QSHJOBLIST) command creates an outfile that lists jobs on the system.
By default all jobs are listed. A filter can be used to list only the jobs you want. The command uses the
QSYS2.ACTIVE_JOB_INFO SQL service. If the SQL fails you may be missing the PTF groups that the service
needs.
:p.The following example lists the jobs named ADMIN to the default outfile QTEMP/JOBTMP0001:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHJOBLIST QRYFILTER('JOBNAME LIKE ''ADMIN''')
           OUTFILE(QTEMP/JOBTMP0001)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHJOBLIST/QRYFILTER'.
Job info query filter (QRYFILTER) - Help
:xh3.Job info query filter (QRYFILTER)
:p.Specifies the SQL selection that picks the jobs to list. It is used as the WHERE condition on the job
information. A quote inside the filter must be entered as two quotes.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.JOBNAME LIKE '%%':epk.
:pd.All jobs are listed.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All jobs are listed.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the SQL selection. For example JOBNAME LIKE 'ADMIN'. The value can be up to 500 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBLIST/OUTFILE'.
File to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.File to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the file that receives the list of jobs found.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.JOBTMP0001:epk.
:pd.The results are written to file JOBTMP0001.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file to receive the results.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The file is created in library QTEMP.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library for the file.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBLIST/PROMPT'.
Prompt SQL for debug (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt SQL for debug (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SQL statement is prompted before it runs. This is useful for debugging.
Normally the selection should be *NO.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The SQL statement is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The SQL statement is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHJOBACT
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHJOBACT'.
Locate Selected Active Jobs (QSHJOBACT) - Help
:p.The Locate Selected Active Jobs (QSHJOBACT) command finds the active jobs that match a filter and counts
them.
Use it to learn how many instances of a job name or generic name are active. This is useful after you start
a subsystem or application shutdown and need to know when all of the named jobs have ended.
The count is placed in data area QTEMP/JOBACTCNT. The command uses the QSYS2.ACTIVE_JOB_INFO SQL service.
If the SQL fails you may be missing the PTF groups that the service needs.
:p.The following example counts the active jobs named ADMIN and does not send an error if none are found:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHJOBACT QRYFILTER('JOBNAME LIKE ''ADMIN''')
          EMPTYERROR(*NO)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example sends an error unless exactly 3 jobs are found:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHJOBACT QRYFILTER('JOBNAME LIKE ''ADMIN''')
          EXPJOBFND(3)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHJOBACT/QRYFILTER'.
Job info query filter (QRYFILTER) - Help
:xh3.Job info query filter (QRYFILTER)
:p.Specifies the SQL selection that picks the active jobs to count. It is used as the WHERE condition on the
job information. A quote inside the filter must be entered as two quotes.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.JOBNAME LIKE 'MYJOB':epk.
:pd.Jobs named MYJOB are counted.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All active jobs are counted.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the SQL selection. For example JOBNAME LIKE 'ADMIN%'. The value can be up to 500 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBACT/MAXJOBFND'.
Max number of jobs found (MAXJOBFND) - Help
:xh3.Max number of jobs found (MAXJOBFND)
:p.Specifies the largest number of matching jobs that is allowed. If more jobs are found a CPF9898 escape
message is sent.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NOLIMIT:epk.
:pd.There is no limit to the number of jobs found.
:pt.:pv.number:epv.
:pd.Enter the maximum number of jobs allowed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBACT/EXPJOBFND'.
Expected number of jobs found (EXPJOBFND) - Help
:xh3.Expected number of jobs found (EXPJOBFND)
:p.Specifies the exact number of matching jobs that is expected. If a different number of jobs is found
a CPF9898 escape message is sent.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NOLIMIT:epk.
:pd.Any number of jobs is accepted.
:pt.:pv.number:epv.
:pd.Enter the number of jobs expected.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBACT/OUTFILE'.
File to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.File to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the file that receives the list of jobs found.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. The name JOBTMP0001 cannot be used because the command uses it for its own work file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.JOBTMPA001:epk.
:pd.The results are written to file JOBTMPA001.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file to receive the results.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The file is created in library QTEMP.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library for the file.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHJOBACT/EMPTYERROR'.
Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR) - Help
:xh3.Escape error if no result data (EMPTYERROR)
:p.Specifies whether an escape message is sent when no jobs match the filter.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.A CPF9898 escape message is sent if no matching jobs are found.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.No escape message is sent when no jobs are found.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHCALL
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHCALL'.
Run Qshell Command Line (QSHCALL) - Help
:p.The Run Qshell Command Line (QSHCALL) command runs a QSH/PASE command line and returns up to 10 values to
CL variables. It works like the QSHEXEC command, but it is meant for CL, RPG and COBOL programmers who are
used
to calling programs and getting values back through parameters. The values come from lines that the command
or script writes to STDOUT that start with RETURNPARM01&colon. to RETURNPARM10&colon..
:p.The command must be run from a CL program because it returns values in CL variables.
:p.The following example runs a Python script and returns two values:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DCL VAR(&amp.RETURN01) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(255)
DCL VAR(&amp.RETURN02) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(255)
QSHCALL CMDLINE('python3 /qshpython/pycallparm1.py')
        DSPSTDOUT(*NO)
        RETURN01(&amp.RETURN01)
        RETURN02(&amp.RETURN02)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHCALL/CMDLINE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CMDLINE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/OUTFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/OUTFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/MBROPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/MBROPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/PASEJOBNAM'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PASEJOBNAM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/RETURN01'.
Return parm 1 (255) (RETURN01) - Help
:xh3.Return parm 1 (255) (RETURN01)
:p.Specifies a CL variable that receives a value that was written to STDOUT by the command or script that
ran.
Up to 10 values can be returned. To return a value, the command or script writes a line to STDOUT that
starts with the keyword :hp2.RETURNPARMxx&colon.:ehp2. followed by the value, where xx is 01 to 10.
:XMP.
:hp2.
RETURNPARM01&colon.my first value
RETURNPARM02&colon.my second value
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The value from the line that starts with RETURNPARM01&colon. is returned in RETURN01, the value from
RETURNPARM02&colon.
is returned in RETURN02, and so on. The variables are set to blanks before the command runs. If a keyword is
not written to STDOUT the matching variable stays blank.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. The command must be run from a CL program because the values are returned in CL
variables.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of a character CL variable with a length of 255.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/RETURN02'.
Return parm 2 (255) (RETURN02) - Help
:xh3.Return parm 2 (255) (RETURN02)
:p.Specifies a CL variable that receives a value that was written to STDOUT by the command or script that
ran.
Up to 10 values can be returned. To return a value, the command or script writes a line to STDOUT that
starts with the keyword :hp2.RETURNPARMxx&colon.:ehp2. followed by the value, where xx is 01 to 10.
:XMP.
:hp2.
RETURNPARM01&colon.my first value
RETURNPARM02&colon.my second value
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The value from the line that starts with RETURNPARM01&colon. is returned in RETURN01, the value from
RETURNPARM02&colon.
is returned in RETURN02, and so on. The variables are set to blanks before the command runs. If a keyword is
not written to STDOUT the matching variable stays blank.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. The command must be run from a CL program because the values are returned in CL
variables.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of a character CL variable with a length of 255.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHCALL/RETURN03'.
Return parm 3 (255) (RETURN03) - Help
:xh3.Return parm 3 (255) (RETURN03)
:p.Specifies a CL variable that receives a value that was written to STDOUT by the command or script that
