.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHGETPARM
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHGETPARM'.
Scan Qshell Log for Parm Vals (QSHGETPARM) - Help
:p.The Scan Qshell Log for Parm Vals (QSHGETPARM) command reads the STDOUT results of the last QSH/PASE
command that was run and returns up to 10 values to CL variables. The command looks in the temporary
STDOUT file QTEMP/STDOUTQSH for lines that start with RETURNPARM01&colon. to RETURNPARM10&colon..
:p.Use it after a command such as QSHEXEC when you did not use QSHCALL but still need values from the
output.
The command must be run from a CL program because it returns values in CL variables.
:p.The following example runs a script and then returns the first value from its output:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DCL VAR(&amp.RETURN01) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(255)
QSHEXEC CMDLINE('python3 /qshpython/pycallparm1.py')
QSHGETPARM RETURN01(&amp.RETURN01)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHGETPARM/RETURN01'.
