.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHGETPR2
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHGETPR2'.
Scan Qshell Log for Parm Vals (QSHGETPR2) - Help
:p.The Scan Qshell Log for Parm Vals (QSHGETPR2) command works like QSHGETPARM. It reads the STDOUT results
of the last QSH/PASE command that was run and returns up to 10 values to CL variables. It also can write the
values to the job log and to data areas so that they can be used by other programs and jobs.
The command looks in the temporary STDOUT file QTEMP/STDOUTQSH for lines that start with
RETURNPARM01&colon. to RETURNPARM10&colon..
:p.The command must be run from a CL program because it returns values in CL variables.
:p.The following example returns the values and also writes them to data areas RTNPARM01 to RTNPARM10 in
QTEMP:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DCL VAR(&amp.RETURN01) TYPE(*CHAR) LEN(255)
QSHEXEC CMDLINE('python3 /qshpython/pycallparm1.py')
QSHGETPR2 RETURN01(&amp.RETURN01)
          WRTDTAARA(*YES)
          DTAARALIB(QTEMP)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHGETPR2/RETURN01'.
Return parm 1 (255) (RETURN01) - Help
:xh3.Return parm 1 (255) (RETURN01)
