.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHPHPRUN
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHPHPRUN'.
Run PHP Script via Qshell (QSHPHPRUN) - Help
:p.The Run PHP Script via Qshell (QSHPHPRUN) command runs a PHP command line (CLI) script with the QSHEXEC
command and logs the results appropriately. The command puts together the PHP command line from the script
directory, script file name and arguments.
:p.The following example runs a PHP script with two arguments:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHPHPRUN SCRIPTDIR('/qshphp')
          SCRIPTFILE('hello.php')
          ARGS('My Parm Value 1' 'My Parm Value 2')
          DSPSTDOUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHPHPRUN/SCRIPTDIR'.
PHP script directory (SCRIPTDIR) - Help
:xh3.PHP script directory (SCRIPTDIR)
:p.Specifies the IFS directory that contains the PHP script.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the IFS directory path. For example /qshphp.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/CHGSCRDIR'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CHGSCRDIR'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/PHPCMD'.
PHP command (PHPCMD) - Help
:xh3.PHP command (PHPCMD)
:p.Specifies the PHP command that is run.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DEFAULT:epk.
:pd.The php command is run as normal.
:pt.:pk.*DEBUG:epk.
:pd.The command php -d error_log= is run so that PHP errors are captured in the STDOUT logging output.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter your own PHP command.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/SCRIPTFILE'.
PHP script file name (SCRIPTFILE) - Help
:xh3.PHP script file name (SCRIPTFILE)
:p.Specifies the PHP script file name without the directory path. The command puts the directory and
file name together.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the script file name. For example hello.php.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/ARGS'.
PHP command line arguments (ARGS) - Help
:xh3.PHP command line arguments (ARGS)
:p.Specifies the command line arguments that are passed to the PHP script. Up to 40 arguments of up to
200 characters each can be passed. Each argument is trimmed automatically.
:p.Do not put double quotes around the arguments unless you use ARGDLM(*NONE), because the command adds the
delimiter for you and extra quotes can change the value that the script receives.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the argument value.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LIST'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/ARGDLM'.
Command line arg delimiter (ARGDLM) - Help
:xh3.Command line arg delimiter (ARGDLM)
:p.Specifies the delimiter that is automatically placed around each command line argument value.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DBLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Double quotes are placed around each argument.
:pt.:pk.*SGLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Single quotes are placed around each argument.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No delimiter is added. Use this when you want to control exactly where quotes are placed in your
arguments.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/PHPPATH'.
PHP bin path (PHPPATH) - Help
:xh3.PHP bin path (PHPPATH)
:p.Specifies the directory path to the PHP binary.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DEFAULT:epk.
:pd.The path stored in the PHPPATH data area in library QSHONI is used. If there is no value
the php command is found using the PATH.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the directory that contains the PHP binary. For example
/QOpenSys/pkgs/bin.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/PRTSTDOUT'.
Prt standard output on errors (PRTSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Prt standard output on errors (PRTSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether to print STDOUT to a spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not print STDOUT.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Print STDOUT to spool.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPHPRUN/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
