:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command DB2UTIL
.************************************************************************
:help name='DB2UTIL'.
Execute db2util Query to IFS (DB2UTIL) - Help
:p.The Execute db2util Query to IFS (DB2UTIL) command runs an SQL statement with the open source db2util
utility and writes the result to an IFS file as JSON, CSV or space delimited text. The db2util command is
run
with the QSHBASH command, so the standard output logging options of that command are also available.
:p.The following example writes the result of a query to a JSON file as an array:
:XMP.
:hp2.
DB2UTIL SQL('select * from qiws.qcustcdt')
        OUTPUTFMT('json')
        JSONFMT('array')
        OUTPUTFILE('/tmp/qcustcdt.json')
        OPTION(*REPLACE)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='DB2UTIL/SQL'.
SQL to execute (SQL) - Help
:xh3.SQL to execute (SQL)
:p.Specifies the SQL statement that db2util runs.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the SQL statement. The statement can be up to 1024 characters.
The statement is enclosed in double quotes on the command line, so avoid double quotes in the SQL.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/OUTPUTFMT'.
SQL to execute (OUTPUTFMT) - Help
:xh3.SQL to execute (OUTPUTFMT)
:p.Specifies the format of the result that is written to the output file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.json:epk.
:pd.The result is written as JSON.
:pt.:pk.csv:epk.
:pd.The result is written as comma separated values.
:pt.:pk.space:epk.
:pd.The result is written as space delimited values.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/JSONFMT'.
JSON output format (JSONFMT) - Help
:xh3.JSON output format (JSONFMT)
:p.Specifies how the JSON result is laid out. This is only used when the output format is json.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.object:epk.
:pd.Each row is written as a JSON object.
:pt.:pk.array:epk.
:pd.The rows are written as a JSON array.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/OUTPUTFILE'.
Output IFS file (OUTPUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Output IFS file (OUTPUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file that receives the result of the query.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name. The command ends with an error if no file name is entered.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/OPTION'.
IFS file option (OPTION) - Help
:xh3.IFS file option (OPTION)
:p.Specifies what happens when the output file already exists.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*REPLACE:epk.
:pd.The existing file is deleted and replaced by the new result.
:pt.:pk.*ADD:epk.
:pd.The new result is added to the end of the existing file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/SETPKGPATH'.
Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys yum package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/VIEWOUTPUT'.
View output file (VIEWOUTPUT) - Help
:xh3.View output file (VIEWOUTPUT)
:p.Specifies whether the output file is shown when the query is done.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The output file is not shown.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The output file is shown on an interactive 5250 session.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/DSPSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/LOGSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/DLTSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/IFSSTDOUT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/IFSFILE'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/IFSOPT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/CCSID'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTSPLF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTUSRDTA'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTHOLD'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.
:help name='DB2UTIL/PASEJOBNAM'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PASEJOBNAM'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command QSHQRYAID
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHQRYAID'.
SQL Add Unique ID Col to Table (QSHQRYAID) - Help
:p.The SQL Add Unique ID Col to Table (QSHQRYAID) command adds a unique ID column to an outfile that was
created by the QSHQRYTMP or QSHQRYSRC command. The column is a big integer identity column that starts with
1.
Use it when you did not ask for the ID column when the outfile was created.
:p.The following example adds a column named RECID to the default outfile QTEMP/SQLTMP0001:
:XMP.
:hp2.
QSHQRYAID OUTFILE(QTEMP/SQLTMP0001)
          IDCOLNAME(RECID)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='QSHQRYAID/OUTFILE'.
Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Temp file to receive results (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies the file that the unique ID column is added to.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.SQLTMP0001:epk.
:pd.The column is added to file SQLTMP0001.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The file is in library QTEMP.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the file is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYAID/IDCOLNAME'.
Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME) - Help
:xh3.Record ID column name (IDCOLNAME)
:p.Specifies the name of the identity column that is added to the file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.RECID:epk.
:pd.The column is named RECID.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the column name. The name can be up to 30 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYAID/PROMPT'.
Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the RUNSQL command is prompted before it runs. Only use this on an interactive
5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The RUNSQL command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The RUNSQL command is prompted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command RUNSQLPRM
.************************************************************************
:help name='RUNSQLPRM'.
Run SQL Action with SQL Stmt (RUNSQLPRM) - Help
:p.The Run SQL Action with SQL Stmt (RUNSQLPRM) command runs an SQL action statement, such as INSERT,
UPDATE, DELETE or CREATE, after placeholder values are replaced in the statement. This is useful for running
variable SQL statements from a CL program. The command uses the RUNSQL command internally.
:p.Placeholders can be any text that is unique, such as :hp2.@@LIB:ehp2.. A quote in the SQL can be provided
through a placeholder, for example :hp2.@@QT:ehp2. with a value of two single quotes.
:p.The following example inserts a record into QIWS/QCUSTCDT by passing an SQL template and values:
:XMP.
:hp2.
RUNSQLPRM SQL('INSERT INTO @@LIB.@@FILE (CUSNUM,LSTNAM)
               VALUES(@@CUSNUM,@@QT@@LSTNAM@@QT)')
          PARMS(@@LIB @@FILE @@CUSNUM @@LSTNAM @@QT)
          PARMVALS(QIWS QCUSTCDT 123456 Test '''')
          NAMING(*SQL)
          DSPOUTPUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='RUNSQLPRM/SQL'.
SQL query (SQL) - Help
:xh3.SQL query (SQL)
:p.Specifies the SQL action statement to run. The statement can contain placeholders that are replaced
with the values from PARMS and PARMVALS.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the SQL statement. The statement can be up to 5000 characters.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/PARMS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/PARMVALS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMVALS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/PROMPT'.
Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the RUNSQL command is prompted before it runs. This is useful for testing. Only use
this on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The RUNSQL command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The RUNSQL command is prompted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/COMMIT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLCOMMIT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/NAMING'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLNAMING'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/OPTION'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLOPTION'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/SECLVLTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLSECLVLTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/DSPOUTPUT'.
Display output output report (DSPOUTPUT) - Help
:xh3.Display output output report (DSPOUTPUT)
:p.Specifies whether the output report of the SQL run is displayed when the SQL ends.
Only use this on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The output report is not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The output report is displayed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/SPLF'.
Print source spool file name (SPLF) - Help
:xh3.Print source spool file name (SPLF)
:p.Specifies the name of the spool file for the listing of the SQL run.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.RUNSQLPRMP:epk.
:pd.The spool file is named RUNSQLPRMP.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the spool file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/USRDTA'.
Print source user data (USRDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print source user data (USRDTA)
:p.Specifies the user data that is stored with the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.RUNSQLPRM:epk.
:pd.The user data is RUNSQLPRM.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user data of up to 10 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/USRDFNDTA'.
Print user defined data (USRDFNDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print user defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:p.Specifies the user defined data that is stored with the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.RUNSQLPRM:epk.
:pd.The user defined data is RUNSQLPRM.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user defined data of up to 255 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLPRM/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command RUNSQLSRC
.************************************************************************
:help name='RUNSQLSRC'.
Run SQL Action from Qry Source (RUNSQLSRC) - Help
:p.The Run SQL Action from Qry Source (RUNSQLSRC) command runs the SQL statements stored in a source member
after placeholder values are replaced in the SQL. This is useful for running variable SQL action statements
and
commands from a CL program. The command uses the RUNSQLSTM command internally.
:p.By default comment lines are removed from a temporary copy of the source before the SQL runs. This lets
you
store SQL that you wrote in ACS, with its comments, in a source member. A comment line must start with
:hp2.--:ehp2. in the first positions of the line. See the DLTCMTLINE parameter. Test your SQL after changing
how comments are handled.
:p.The following example runs the SQL in member SQLTEST4 with replacement values:
:XMP.
:hp2.
RUNSQLSRC SRCFILE(QSHONI/SOURCE)
          SRCMBR(SQLTEST4)
          PARMS(@@LIB @@FILE @@CUSNUM @@LSTNAM)
          PARMVALS(QIWS QCUSTCDT 123456 Test)
          NAMING(*SQL)
          DSPOUTPUT(*YES)
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='RUNSQLSRC/SRCFILE'.
SQL source file (SRCFILE) - Help
:xh3.SQL source file (SRCFILE)
:p.Specifies the source physical file that contains the SQL source member.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.source-file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the source file.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the source file.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the source file is located.
:EPARML.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/SRCMBR'.
Source member (SRCMBR) - Help
:xh3.Source member (SRCMBR)
:p.Specifies the source member that contains the SQL to run.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.source-member-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the source member.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/PARMS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/PARMVALS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMVALS'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/PROMPT'.
Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT) - Help
:xh3.Prompt RUNSQL (PROMPT)
:p.Specifies whether the SQL command is prompted before it runs. This is useful for testing. Only use
this on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The command is prompted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/DLTTMPSRC'.
Delete temp source file after (DLTTMPSRC) - Help
:xh3.Delete temp source file after (DLTTMPSRC)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary source member that is created to run the SQL is deleted afterward.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is deleted.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is not deleted. Use this to review it for troubleshooting.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/COMMIT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLCOMMIT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/NAMING'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLNAMING'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/OPTION'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLOPTION'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/OUTPUT'.
Listing output (OUTPUT) - Help
:xh3.Listing output (OUTPUT)
:p.Specifies where the listing of the SQL run is sent.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No listing is produced.
:pt.:pk.*ERROR:epk.
:pd.A listing is produced only if errors occur.
:pt.:pk.*NOLIST:epk.
:pd.No listing is produced.
:pt.:pk.*MSG:epk.
:pd.Messages are sent to the job log.
:pt.:pk.*PRINT:epk.
:pd.The listing is printed to a spool file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/SECLVLTXT'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLSECLVLTXT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/DSPOUTPUT'.
Display output output report (DSPOUTPUT) - Help
:xh3.Display output output report (DSPOUTPUT)
:p.Specifies whether the output report of the SQL run is displayed when the SQL ends.
Only use this on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The output report is not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The output report is displayed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/DLTCMTLINE'.
Del comment line from temp src (DLTCMTLINE) - Help
:xh3.Del comment line from temp src (DLTCMTLINE)
:p.Specifies whether comment lines are removed from the temporary copy of the source member before the SQL
runs.
A comment line must have :hp2.--:ehp2. at the start of the trimmed line. Text that contains :hp2.--:ehp2.
anywhere else in a line, such as in a text constant, is not changed.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Comment lines are removed, and lines that are empty after the comment text is removed are also removed.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The source member is used as it is and comments are not removed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/DSPTMPSRC'.
Display temp source member (DSPTMPSRC) - Help
:xh3.Display temp source member (DSPTMPSRC)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary source member is displayed after it is prepared. This lets you preview
the SQL that will actually run after comments were removed and values were replaced. It is good for
troubleshooting.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is displayed on an interactive 5250 session.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/PRTTMPSRC'.
Print temp source member (PRTTMPSRC) - Help
:xh3.Print temp source member (PRTTMPSRC)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary source member is printed after it is prepared. The spool file name,
user data and user defined data are set by the SPLF, USRDTA and USRDFNDTA parameters.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is not printed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is printed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/SPLF'.
Print source spool file name (SPLF) - Help
:xh3.Print source spool file name (SPLF)
:p.Specifies the name of the spool file for the printed temporary source member.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.RUNSQLSRCP:epk.
:pd.The spool file is named RUNSQLSRCP.
:pt.:pk.*SRCMBR:epk.
:pd.The source member name is used as the spool file name.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the spool file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/USRDTA'.
Print source user data (USRDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print source user data (USRDTA)
:p.Specifies the user data that is stored with the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SRCMBR:epk.
:pd.The source member name is used as the user data.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user data of up to 10 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/USRDFNDTA'.
Print user defined data (USRDFNDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print user defined data (USRDFNDTA)
:p.Specifies the user defined data that is stored with the spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SRCMBR:epk.
:pd.The source member name is used as the user defined data.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the user defined data of up to 255 characters.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='RUNSQLSRC/PRTOUTQ'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPRTOUTQ'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Primary Help for command WRKIFSLIST
.************************************************************************
:help name='WRKIFSLIST'.
List IFS Files (WRKIFSLIST) - Help
:p.The List IFS Files (WRKIFSLIST) command shows an interactive list of the files and directories in an
IFS directory. It is a customizable alternative to the Work with Links (WRKLNK) command. The list is
built with the IFS SQL services.
:p.Type an option next to an entry and press Enter. The options are shown at the top of the display:
:XMP.
:hp2.
2=Edit  3=Copy  4=Del  5=View  7=Rename  8=Attr  9=Auth
10=Move  13=ChgAtr  VFY=Vfy SAVF  RST=Rst Lib SAVF
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following function keys can be used:
:XMP.
:hp2.
F3=Exit
F5=Refresh
F8=Home Dir
F10=Display Joblog
F12=Move back one directory level
F21=Command line
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The following example lists the files in directory /home/user1:
:XMP.
:hp2.
WRKIFSLIST IFSDIR('/home/user1')
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:ehelp.

:help name='WRKIFSLIST/IFSDIR'.
IFS directory (IFSDIR) - Help
:xh3.IFS directory (IFSDIR)
:p.Specifies the IFS directory whose files and directories are listed.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the directory.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

.************************************************************************
.*  Additional parameter help for QSHQRYTMP, QSHQRYSRC and QSHPYRUN
.************************************************************************
:help name='QSHQRYTMP/CPYRESULTS'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYRESULTS'.
:ehelp.
