:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CPYFMBROPT'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/PROMPTCPYF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/PROMPTCPYF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/CLRAFTCPYF'.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/CLRAFTCPYF'.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/DLTCMTLINE'.
Del comment line from temp src (DLTCMTLINE) - Help
:xh3.Del comment line from temp src (DLTCMTLINE)
:p.Specifies whether comment lines are removed from the temporary copy of the SQL source member before the
query runs. A comment line must have :hp2.--:ehp2. at the start of the trimmed line. The delimiter
:hp2.--//:ehp2. can also be used anywhere in a line, and the data after the delimiter is removed. Text that
contains :hp2.--:ehp2. anywhere else in a line, such as in a text constant, is not changed.
:p.The command does more than run an SQL statement, because it creates a table from the query, so comments
must
be removed at run time. Test your queries after changing how comments are handled.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Comment lines are removed, and lines that are empty after the comment text is removed are also removed.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The source member is used as it is and comments are not removed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHQRYSRC/DSPTMPSRC'.
Display temp source member (DSPTMPSRC) - Help
:xh3.Display temp source member (DSPTMPSRC)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary source member is displayed after it is prepared. This lets you preview
the SQL that will actually run after comments were removed and values were replaced. It is good for
troubleshooting.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary source member is displayed on an interactive 5250 session.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/VENVPATH'.
Virtual environment base path (VENVPATH) - Help
:xh3.Virtual environment base path (VENVPATH)
:p.Specifies the IFS path of the Python virtual environment. This is only used when USEVENV(*YES) is
specified.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the base path of the virtual environment.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/SKIPDEACT'.
Skip virtual env deactivate (SKIPDEACT) - Help
:xh3.Skip virtual env deactivate (SKIPDEACT)
:p.Specifies whether the virtual environment deactivate step is skipped. This is only used when a virtual
environment is used. If the virtual environment is used with QShell there is no deactivate command
available,
so the deactivate fails unless *YES is selected.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The virtual environment deactivate step is skipped.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The virtual environment is deactivated after the script runs.
:eparml.
:ehelp.
:help name='QSHPYRUN/USEBASH'.
Use bash instead of QShell (USEBASH) - Help
:xh3.Use bash instead of QShell (USEBASH)
:p.Specifies whether the Python script is run with bash instead of QShell.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The script is run with the QSHBASH command.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The script is run with the QSHEXEC command.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*****************************************************************
.*  COMMON HELP
.*
.*  Common help text modules (can be embedded elsewhere)
.*
.*****************************************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/ASTERISK'.
:NT.
Do not precede an entry with an asterisk unless that entry is a
"special value" that is shown (on the display itself or in the help
information) with an asterisk.
:ENT.
:EHELP.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/NOPARMS'.
:P.
There are no parameters for this command.
:EHELP.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/LIST'.
:P.
You can enter multiple values for this parameter.  If you are on an
entry display and you need additional entry fields to enter these
multiple values, type a plus sign (+) in the entry field opposite
the phrase "+ for more", and press the Enter key.
:EHELP.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/LOGGINGNOTE'.
:P.
:hp3.STDOUT Logging Note::ehp3.
During execution, the CL command always creates a temporary outfile in
library QTEMP that gets automatically populated with standard output (STDOUT) from the
QSH/PASE command process that gets run.
The temporary STDOUT output file name is: :hp2.QTEMP/STDOUTQSH:ehp2..
:p.
If the file already exists for a subsequent run of the command, the :hp2.QTEMP/STDOUTQSH:ehp2.
temporary file is automatically cleared before
running so each run gets a fresh copy of :hp2.QTEMP/STDOUTQSH:ehp2..
The :hp2.QTEMP/STDOUTQSH:ehp2. temp file gets created automatically always,
even if none of the switches such as: :hp2.DSPSTDOUT, LOGSTDOUT, PRTSTDOUT or IFSSTDOUT:ehp2.
are specified.
:EHELP.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used across many
.*   QshOni commands.
.*
.*******************************************
.*   Help for parameter CMDLINE
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/CMDLINE'.
QSH command line (CMDLINE) - Help
:xh3.QSH command line (CMDLINE)
:p.Specifies the Qshell/PASE command line sequence to run. Semicolons can chain commands.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter a valid Qshell or PASE command, or script filename if in PATH.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SETPKGPATH'.
Set package path (SETPKGPATH) - Help
:xh3.Set QOpenSys package path (SETPKGPATH)
:p.Specifies whether to prepend /QOpenSys/pkgs/bin to PATH.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Include package path.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not include package path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/DSPSTDOUT'.
Display STDOUT (DSPSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Display standard output result (DSPSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether to display the STDOUT results on the terminal.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not display STDOUT.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Display STDOUT.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/DLTSTDOUT'.
Delete STDOUT IFS file (DLTSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Delete standard output result (DLTSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether to delete temporary IFS STDOUT files after run.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Delete IFS STDOUT files.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Keep IFS STDOUT files.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/IFSSTDOUT'.
Copy STDOUT to IFS (IFSSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Copy std output to IFS file (IFSSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether to copy STDOUT to an IFS file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not copy STDOUT to IFS.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Copy STDOUT to IFS.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/IFSFILE'.
IFS file (IFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.IFS file for STDOUT results (IFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the path of the IFS file to receive STDOUT output.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter full IFS file path.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/IFSOPT'.
IFS file option (IFSOPT) - Help
:xh3.IFS file option (IFSOPT)
:p.Specifies action if IFS file exists: replace, add, or fail.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*REPLACE:epk.
:pd.Overwrite existing file.
:pt.:pk.*ADD:epk.
:pd.Append to file.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.Fail if exists.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID'.
Coded character set ID for job (CCSID) - Help
:xh3.Coded character set ID for job (CCSID)
:p.When using the iToolkit component for command access, I originally had some issues with CL commands not
working correctly. However I don't currently remember exactly why. This may have been solved, however I
recommend still passing unless you are in a non US country.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SAME:epk.
:pd.If you set to *SAME, the CCSID will stay the same as your current job with no change.
:pt.:pk.1-65535:epk.
:pd.Specify the CCSID.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/LOGSTDOUT'.
Log STDOUT (LOGSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Log standard output to job log (LOGSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether STDOUT is written to the job log.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not log STDOUT.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Write STDOUT log entries into the current job's job log.
Use this if you want the log info in the IBM i joblog.
All STDOUT entries are written as CPF message: :hp2.QSS9898:ehp2.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSTDOUT'.
Print STDOUT (PRTSTDOUT) - Help
:xh3.Print standard output result (PRTSTDOUT)
:p.Specifies whether to print STDOUT to a spool file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not print STDOUT.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Print STDOUT to spool.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTSPLF'.
Spool file name (PRTSPLF) - Help
:xh3.Print STDOUT spool file (PRTSPLF)
:p.Specifies spool file name for printed STDOUT.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter spool file name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTUSRDTA'.
Spool user data (PRTUSRDTA) - Help
:xh3.Print STDOUT user data (PRTUSRDTA)
:p.Specifies user data for spool generated by PRTSTDOUT.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter user data or none.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTTXT'.
Spool text (PRTTXT) - Help
:xh3.Print STDOUT print text (PRTTXT)
:p.Specifies descriptive text for spool file by PRTSTDOUT.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter descriptive text.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTHOLD'.
Hold spool (PRTHOLD) - Help
:xh3.Print STDOUT hold spool file (PRTHOLD)
:p.Specifies whether generated spool is held or released.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Hold spool file.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Release spool file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRTOUTQ'.
Output queue (PRTOUTQ) - Help
:xh3.Print STDOUT to outq (PRTOUTQ)
:p.Specifies the output queue for spool by PRTSTDOUT.
:P.
The possible values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.
The STDOUT spool file is placed on the job's output queue.
:PT.:PK.ouptput-queue-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name (library-name/output-queue-name) of the output
queue on which the STDOUT spool file is placed.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the output queue name.
:PT.:PK.library-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the output queue is located.
:EPARML.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/OUTFILE'.
Output file (OUTFILE) - Help
:xh3.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:p.Specifies database file to receive STDOUT or SQL results.
:P.
The possible values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.STDOUTQSH:EPK.
:PD.
The database file to STDOUT spool file is placed on the job's output queue.
:PT.:PK.database-file-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name (library-name/database-file-name) of the outfile.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The QTEMP library is used.
:PT.:PK.library-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the outfile is located.
:EPARML.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/MBROPT'.
Member option (MBROPT) - Help
:xh3.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:p.Specifies replace or add records in output file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*REPLACE:epk.
:pd.Replace existing records.
:pt.:pk.*ADD:epk.
:pd.Add records to file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PASEJOBNAM'.
PASE job name (PASEJOBNAM) - Help
:xh3.PASE fork thread job names (PASEJOBNAM)
:p.Set PASE_FORK_JOBNAME environment variable to set forked thread jobs
to have a unique name other than QP0ZSPWP which is the default.
Set the value or *DEFAULT=QP0ZSPWP.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DEFAULT:epk.
:pd.Use QP0ZSPWP as default PASE job name.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter a custom PASE job name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CRTIDCOL'.
Create identity column (CRTIDCOL) - Help
:xh3.Create identity column (CRTIDCOL)
:p.Specifies whether to add identity column to outfile.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Do not add identity column.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Add identity column.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/JRN'.
Journal name (JRN) - Help
:xh3.Journal name (JRN)
:p.Specifies the journal to receive journal entries.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.name:epv.
:pd.Enter journal name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/JRNRCV'.
Journal receiver name (JRNRCV) - Help
:xh3.Journal receiver name (JRNRCV)
:p.Specifies the journal receiver for the journal.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.name:epv.
:pd.Enter receiver name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SETENV'.
Set environment (SETENV) - Help
:xh3.Set shell environment (SETENV)
:p.Specifies whether to enable or disable environment wrapper.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Enable environment setup.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Disable environment setup.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/OWNER'.
IFS file owner (OWNER) - Help
:xh3.Owner for IFS object (OWNER)
:p.Specifies owner profile for IFS file or directory.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter user profile name.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/AUT'.
Authority for IFS (AUT) - Help
:xh3.IFS authority setting (AUT)
:p.Specifies authority for IFS file or directory (e.g., *RWX, *RX).
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*RX:epk.
:pd.Read/Execute only.
:pt.:pk.*RWX:epk.
:pd.Read, Write, Execute.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/LOGTYPE'.
Log type (LOGTYPE) - Help
:xh3.Log type selector (LOGTYPE)
:p.Specifies log view: summary or detail.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SUMMARY:epk.
:pd.Summary view.
:pt.:pk.*DETAIL:epk.
:pd.Detailed view.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SYMLNKTO'.
Symbolic link target (SYMLNKTO) - Help
:xh3.Symbolic link target path (SYMLNKTO)
:p.Specifies IFS target path for symlink.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter full IFS path of target.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/ERRMSGID'.
Error message file ID (ERRMSGID) - Help
:xh3.Error message identifier (ERRMSGID)
:p.Specifies message identifier to simulate an error.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter CPF or user-defined message ID.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SRCFILE'.
Source file (SRCFILE) - Help
:xh3.Source file where QShell/PASE/Bash script is stored.
:p.Specifies source physical file containing QShell/PASE/Bash script.
:P.
The possible values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.
??? UNKNOWN ???
:PT.:PK.source-physical-file-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name (library-name/source-physical-file-name) of the source file.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.library-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the source physical file is located.
:EPARML.
:EPARML.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.


:HELP NAME='COMMON/SRCMBR'.
Source member (SRCMBR) - Help
:xh3.Source member where QShell/PASE script is stored.
:p.Specifies source member containing QShell/PASE script.
:P.
The possible values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.source-member-name:EPK.
:PD.
Specify the member name in the source file.
:EPARML.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CMDPARM'.
:p.Specifies the command line parms to pass to the selected script that runs.
If no parameters are needed, simply pass ' ' for the CMDPARM value.
:P.
Parameters can be delimited with double quotes if needed.
Ex: "parm1" "parm2" "parm3"
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/RMVTMPSCR'.
Remove temporary IFS script file (RMVTMPSCR) - Help
:xh3.Remove temporary IFS script file (RMVTMPSCR)
:p.This option determines if the temporary IFS script file is auto-deleted after running.
Normally the selection should be *YES to delete the temp file.
Otherwise specify *NO if you are debugging for some reason.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Deletes the temporary IFS script file after running.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Keeps the temporary IFS script file after running.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PROMPTCMD'.
Prompt Commands (PROMPTCMD) - Help
:xh3.Prompt commands (PROMPTCMD)
:p.This option determines if the QSH command is prompted interactively for testing or
review of the actual QShell command line with parameter values before running the command.
Normally the selection should be *NO since prompting is only needed if testing.
Specify *YES if you are debugging for some reason and want the QSH command to prompt
on an interactive 5250 session before running.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Does not prompt the QSH command for testing or review.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Prompts the QSH command for testing or review before running.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common save/restore parameters
.*   used by the QSHSAV*, QSHRST* and QSHVFYSAVF commands.
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/TGTRLS'.
Target release (TGTRLS) - Help
:xh3.Target release (TGTRLS)
:p.Specifies the release of IBM i on which you intend to restore and use the saved data.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*CURRENT:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on the release of IBM i that is currently running on your system.
:pt.:pk.*PRV:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on the previous release of IBM i that is supported by the current
release.
:pt.:pk.V7R1M0:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on release V7R1M0 of IBM i.
:pt.:pk.V7R2M0:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on release V7R2M0 of IBM i.
:pt.:pk.V7R3M0:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on release V7R3M0 of IBM i.
:pt.:pk.V7R4M0:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on release V7R4M0 of IBM i.
:pt.:pk.V7R5M0:epk.
:pd.The objects are saved for restoring on release V7R5M0 of IBM i.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Specify the release in the format VxRxMx. Any other supported release can be entered.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/UPDHST'.
Update history (UPDHST) - Help
:xh3.Update history (UPDHST)
:p.Specifies whether the save history information of the saved objects is updated.
This is the information shown by the Display Object Description (DSPOBJD) command.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The save date and time are updated for each saved object.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The save history information is not updated.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PRECHK'.
Object pre-check (PRECHK) - Help
:xh3.Object pre-check (PRECHK)
:p.Specifies whether the save operation ends if any selected object cannot be saved.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The save operation does not end if an object cannot be saved. The objects that can be saved are saved.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The save operation ends before anything is saved if any selected object is damaged, locked or otherwise
not saveable.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SAVACT'.
Save active (SAVACT) - Help
:xh3.Save active (SAVACT)
:p.Specifies whether objects that are in use by other jobs can be saved while they are being changed
(save-while-active).
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.Objects that are in use are not saved while they are active.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Objects that are in use can be saved while they are active.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SAVFDTA'.
Save file data (SAVFDTA) - Help
:xh3.Save file data (SAVFDTA)
:p.Specifies whether the data in save files is saved.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The data in any save files found is saved along with the save file objects.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Only the save file objects are saved. The data in the save files is not saved.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SPLFDTA'.
Spooled file data (SPLFDTA) - Help
:xh3.Spooled file data (SPLFDTA)
:p.Specifies whether spooled file data is saved for output queues that are saved.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No spooled file data is saved.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.All spooled file data is saved for the output queues that are saved.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/QDTA'.
Queue data (QDTA) - Help
:xh3.Queue data (QDTA)
:p.Specifies whether the messages in data queues are saved.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.The messages in data queues are not saved. Only the data queue objects are saved.
:pt.:pk.*DTAQ:epk.
:pd.The messages in data queues are saved along with the data queue objects.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/DTACPR'.
Data compression (DTACPR) - Help
:xh3.Data compression (DTACPR)
:p.Specifies whether data compression is used when the data is saved to the temporary save file.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*HIGH:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed using high compression. This gives the smallest save file but takes the longest.
:pt.:pk.*DEV:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed if the device supports compression.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.No data compression is done.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed. The system chooses the compression level.
:pt.:pk.*LOW:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed using low compression. This is the fastest compression.
:pt.:pk.*MEDIUM:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed using medium compression.
:pt.:pk.*ZLIB:epk.
:pd.Data is compressed using the ZLIB compression algorithm.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/DLTTMPSAVF'.
Delete temporary save file (DLTTMPSAVF) - Help
:xh3.Delete temporary save file (DLTTMPSAVF)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary save file in library QTEMP is deleted when the command ends.
Normally the selection should be *YES. Specify *NO if you want to leave the save file around for
testing or to display its contents with the Display Save File (DSPSAVF) command in the same job.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary save file in QTEMP is deleted.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary save file in QTEMP is not deleted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/REPLACESAVF'.
Replace output IFS file (REPLACE) - Help
:xh3.Replace output IFS file (REPLACE)
:p.Specifies whether an existing IFS save file is replaced.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.If the IFS file already exists the command ends with an error and the save is not done.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the IFS file already exists it is deleted and replaced with the new save file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/TOIFSFILE'.
Save to IFS file (TOIFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.Save to IFS file (TOIFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file the save file data is copied to. The result is a standard IBM i save file stored
in the IFS, which makes it easy to transport or back up to a NAS or other storage.
:p.When a special value is used, the file is created in the directory stored in data area
:hp2.QSHONI/SAVFDIR:ehp2.. The data area is created automatically and defaults to :hp2./tmp/savfqsh:ehp2..
You can change the data area value to your own default directory. If the directory does not exist it is
created.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*DATETIME:epk.
:pd.The file name is generated and includes the current date and time. See the command help for the name
format.
:pt.:pk.*DATE:epk.
:pd.The file name is generated and includes the current date. See the command help for the name format.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name. Using a .savf extension is recommended.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/FRMIFSFILE'.
From IFS file (FRMIFSFILE) - Help
:xh3.From IFS file (FRMIFSFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS file that contains the save file data to restore from. This is normally a file
created by one of the QshOni save commands (QSHSAVLIB, QSHSAVOBJ, QSHSAVCHG or QSHSAVIFS).
The file is copied to a temporary save file in QTEMP before the restore is done.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path and file name of the save file.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CLRLIB'.
Clear restore to lib if exists (CLRLIB) - Help
:xh3.Clear restore to lib if exists (CLRLIB)
:p.Specifies whether the library being restored to is cleared first when it already exists.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The library is not cleared. Restored objects are added to or replace objects in the existing library.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.If the library exists all of the objects in it are deleted before the restore is done.
Use with care since the existing objects cannot be recovered.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/RSTLIB'.
Restore to library (RSTLIB) - Help
:xh3.Restore to library (RSTLIB)
:p.Specifies the library the objects are restored into.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SAVLIB:epk.
:pd.The objects are restored into the same library name that they were saved from.
:pt.:pv.library-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the library to restore the objects into.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   remote access and file transfer commands
.*   (QSHSSH, QSHSCP and QSHLFTP).
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/SSHPORT'.
TCP port (PORT) - Help
:xh3.SSH server TCP port
:p.Specifies the TCP/IP port number the SSH server on the remote system listens on.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.22:epk.
:pd.The standard SSH port 22 is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the port number the remote SSH server is using.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SSHKEYFILE'.
SSH private key file (KEYFILE) - Help
:xh3.SSH private key file (KEYFILE)
:p.Specifies the IFS path of the SSH private key file used to sign on to the remote system. The key file
must be readable by the user running the command. A private key is recommended over a password.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NOKEYFILE:epk.
:pd.No private key file is used. The default SSH keys for the user are used or a password is used.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the full IFS path of the private key file. For example /home/user1/.ssh/id_rsa.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/KEYPASSWD'.
SSH private key file password (KEYPASSWD) - Help
:xh3.SSH private key file password (KEYPASSWD)
:p.Specifies the pass phrase of the private key file.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. The value is accepted by the command, but it is not currently used when the SSH
or SFTP command line is built. Use a private key file without a pass phrase, or an SSH agent, until this
is implemented.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NOPASSWORD:epk.
:pd.The private key file does not have a pass phrase.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the pass phrase of the private key file.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   TCP/IP port commands (QSHPORTCHK and QSHPORTEND).
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/LOCALPORT'.
Local port (LOCALPORT) - Help
:xh3.Local port (LOCALPORT)
:p.Specifies the local TCP/IP port number to check.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.1-65535:epv.
:pd.Enter the port number.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CONNTYPE'.
Connection type (CONNTYPE) - Help
:xh3.Connection type (CONNTYPE)
:p.Specifies the type of TCP/IP connection to check.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.IPV4:epk.
:pd.IPv4 connections are checked.
:pt.:pk.IPV6:epk.
:pd.IPv6 connections are checked.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   source member copy commands (QSHCPYSRC and QSHSRCIFS).
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCFILE'.
Source file (SRCFILE) - Help
:xh3.Source file (SRCFILE)
:p.Specifies the source physical file that contains the source member to copy.
:parml.
:pt.:pk.*SAME:epk.
:pd.The source file name used on the last command is used.
:pt.:pv.source-file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the source physical file.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the source file.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the source file is located.
:EPARML.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CPYSRCMBR'.
Source member (SRCMBR) - Help
:xh3.Source member (SRCMBR)
:p.Specifies the source member to copy.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.source-member-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the source member.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/REQPARM'.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   simple log commands (QSHWRTLOG and QSHPRTLOG).
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/LOGFILE'.
To log file (LOGFILE) - Help
:xh3.To log file (LOGFILE)
:p.Specifies the database file that holds the simple log records. Each record holds a time stamp,
a message type and the message text.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.LOGTMP0001:epk.
:pd.The log file is named LOGTMP0001.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the log file.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.QTEMP:EPK.
:PD.
The log file is in library QTEMP, so it only exists for the life of the job.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the log file.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the log file is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   commands that return values (QSHCALL, QSHPYCALL,
.*   QSHGETPARM, QSHGETPR2) and the script commands
.*   (QSHPYCALL, QSHPHPRUN).
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/RETURNPARM'.
Return parm (RETURNxx) - Help
:xh3.Return parm value (RETURNxx)
:p.Specifies a CL variable that receives a value that was written to STDOUT by the command or script that
ran.
Up to 10 values can be returned. To return a value, the command or script writes a line to STDOUT that
starts with the keyword :hp2.RETURNPARMxx&colon.:ehp2. followed by the value, where xx is 01 to 10.
:XMP.
:hp2.
RETURNPARM01&colon.my first value
RETURNPARM02&colon.my second value
:ehp2.
:EXMP.
:p.The value from the line that starts with RETURNPARM01&colon. is returned in RETURN01, the value from
RETURNPARM02&colon.
is returned in RETURN02, and so on. The variables are set to blanks before the command runs. If a keyword is
not written to STDOUT the matching variable stays blank.
:p.:hp3.Note::ehp3. The command must be run from a CL program because the values are returned in CL
variables.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-variable:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of a character CL variable with a length of 255.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/ARGDLM'.
Command line arg delimiter (ARGDLM) - Help
:xh3.Command line argument delimiter (ARGDLM)
:p.Specifies the delimiter that is automatically placed around each command line argument value.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*DBLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Double quotes are placed around each argument.
:pt.:pk.*SGLQUOTE:epk.
:pd.Single quotes are placed around each argument.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No delimiter is added. Use this when you want to control exactly where quotes are placed in your
arguments.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CCSID37'.
Coded character set ID for job (CCSID) - Help
:xh3.Coded character set ID for job (CCSID)
:p.Specifies the CCSID the job uses while the script runs. This affects how the script output is converted.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.37:epk.
:pd.CCSID 37 (US English EBCDIC) is used.
:pt.:pk.*SAME:epk.
:pd.The CCSID stays the same as the current job with no change.
:pt.:pk.1-65535:epk.
:pd.Specify the CCSID.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/DEBUGEXEC'.
Debug QSHEXEC command (DEBUGCMD) - Help
:xh3.Debug QSHEXEC command (DEBUGCMD)
:p.Specifies whether the command line that is built is shown before it runs. The command line is run with
the
QSHEXEC command. This is good for debugging, or if you are curious what the QSHEXEC command will look like.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The command line is not shown.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The command line is prompted on an interactive 5250 session before it runs.
Your job must be running interactively.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CHGSCRDIR'.
Change to script directory (CHGSCRDIR) - Help
:xh3.Change to script directory (CHGSCRDIR)
:p.Specifies whether the current working directory is changed to the script directory before the script
runs.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The current working directory is not changed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The current working directory is changed to the script directory.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   RUNSQLPRM and RUNSQLSRC commands.
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMS'.
SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS) - Help
:xh3.SQL placeholder parm name (PARMS)
:p.Specifies up to 30 placeholder names that are replaced in the SQL at run time. Each placeholder in
this list is replaced by the value in the same position in the PARMVALS list. These are not required
if you do not need replacement values.
:p.Ex: :hp2.@@LIB:ehp2. for a library or :hp2.@@FILE:ehp2. for a file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the placeholder name.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LIST'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPARMVALS'.
SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS) - Help
:xh3.SQL parm replacement value (PARMVALS)
:p.Specifies up to 30 replacement values for the placeholders that are listed in PARMS. The values are
matched to the placeholders by position.
:p.Ex: :hp2.QIWS:ehp2. for a library or :hp2.QCUSTCDT:ehp2. for a file.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.character-value:epv.
:pd.Enter the value that replaces the placeholder.
:eparml.
:P.
:IMHELP NAME='COMMON/LIST'.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLCOMMIT'.
Committment control (COMMIT) - Help
:xh3.Committment control (COMMIT)
:p.Specifies the isolation level, or commitment control level, that the SQL runs with.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NONE:epk.
:pd.Commitment control is not used. Changes are made right away.
:pt.:pk.*NC:epk.
:pd.Same as *NONE. No commit.
:pt.:pk.*CHG:epk.
:pd.Uncommitted changes can be read by other jobs (uncommitted read).
:pt.:pk.*UR:epk.
:pd.Same as *CHG.
:pt.:pk.*CS:epk.
:pd.Cursor stability.
:pt.:pk.*ALL:epk.
:pd.Read stability.
:pt.:pk.*RS:epk.
:pd.Same as *ALL.
:pt.:pk.*RR:epk.
:pd.Repeatable read.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLNAMING'.
Naming (NAMING) - Help
:xh3.Naming (NAMING)
:p.Specifies the naming convention that the SQL uses for objects.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SYS:epk.
:pd.System naming is used. Objects are named library/object.
:pt.:pk.*SQL:epk.
:pd.SQL naming is used. Objects are named schema.object.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLOPTION'.
Source listing options (OPTION) - Help
:xh3.Source listing options (OPTION)
:p.Specifies the listing that is produced when the SQL runs.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*LIST:epk.
:pd.A listing of the SQL and any errors is produced.
:pt.:pk.*NOSRC:epk.
:pd.A listing is produced that does not show the SQL source.
:pt.:pk.*ERRLIST:epk.
:pd.A listing is produced only if errors occur.
:pt.:pk.*NOLIST:epk.
:pd.No listing is produced.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLSECLVLTXT'.
Second level text (SECLVLTXT) - Help
:xh3.Second level text (SECLVLTXT)
:p.Specifies whether the second level message text is included for errors in the listing.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.Second level text is included.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.Second level text is not included.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLDSPOUTPUT'.
Display output report (DSPOUTPUT) - Help
:xh3.Display output report (DSPOUTPUT)
:p.Specifies whether the output report of the SQL run is displayed when the SQL ends.
Only use this on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The output report is not displayed.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The output report is displayed.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/SQLPRTOUTQ'.
Print to outq (PRTOUTQ) - Help
:xh3.Print to outq (PRTOUTQ)
:p.Specifies the output queue that receives the printed listing of the SQL run.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*SAME:epk.
:pd.The listing is placed on the output queue of the job.
:pt.:pv.output-queue-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the output queue.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the output queue.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the output queue is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

.*******************************************
.*   Help for common parameters used by the
.*   result copy options of QSHQRYTMP and QSHQRYSRC.
.*******************************************
:HELP NAME='COMMON/CPYRESULTS'.
Copy results via CPYF (CPYRESULTS) - Help
:xh3.Copy results via CPYF (CPYRESULTS)
:p.Specifies whether the query results are copied to another file with the Copy File (CPYF) command. This is
useful when you run several queries and want to combine their results in one file. By default the command
works as it did before and nothing is copied.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The results are not copied.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The results are copied to the file named by CPYTOFILE.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CPYTOFILE'.
File to receive CPYF results (CPYTOFILE) - Help
:xh3.File to receive CPYF results (CPYTOFILE)
:p.Specifies the file that receives the copied results. This is only used when CPYRESULTS(*YES) is
specified.
:parml.
:pt.:pv.file-name:epv.
:pd.Specify the name of the file.
:eparml.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.
The library list is used to locate the file.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.
Specify the name of the library where the file is located.
:EPARML.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CRTFILE'.
Create results file (CRTFILE) - Help
:xh3.Create results file (CRTFILE)
:p.Specifies whether the file named by CPYTOFILE is created when the results are copied.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The file is created from the query results when it does not exist.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The file is not created. It must already exist.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CPYFMBROPT'.
Replace or add records (MBROPT) - Help
:xh3.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:p.Specifies how the copied records are applied to the file named by CPYTOFILE. These values are the
MBROPT values of the Copy File (CPYF) command.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*ADD:epk.
:pd.The records are added to the end of the file.
:pt.:pk.*REPLACE:epk.
:pd.The existing records are replaced by the copied records.
:pt.:pk.*UPDADD:epk.
:pd.Existing records with matching keys are updated and other records are added.
:pt.:pk.*NONE:epk.
:pd.No member option is specified.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/PROMPTCPYF'.
Prompt the CPYF command (PROMPTCPYF) - Help
:xh3.Prompt the CPYF command (PROMPTCPYF)
:p.Specifies whether the CPYF command is prompted before it runs. This is useful for testing. Only use this
on an interactive 5250 session.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*NO:epk.
:pd.The CPYF command is not prompted.
:pt.:pk.*YES:epk.
:pd.The CPYF command is prompted.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:HELP NAME='COMMON/CLRAFTCPYF'.
Clear temp outfile after CPYF (CLRAFTCPYF) - Help
:xh3.Clear temp outfile after CPYF (CLRAFTCPYF)
:p.Specifies whether the temporary outfile is cleared after the results are copied.
:parml.
:pt.:pk def.*YES:epk.
:pd.The temporary outfile is cleared after the copy.
:pt.:pk.*NO:epk.
:pd.The temporary outfile is not cleared.
:eparml.
:ehelp.

:epnlgrp.
